Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.56,0:00:04.83,EN,,0,0,0,,—What does the Minecraft wiki look like in your mind's eye?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.85,0:00:06.89,EN,,0,0,0,,What do you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.92,0:00:08.30,EN,,0,0,0,,If you see an apple,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.32,0:00:09.82,EN,,0,0,0,,you've done something wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.84,0:00:12.21,EN,,0,0,0,,The game's reliance on the wiki is something that, uh,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.23,0:00:14.18,EN,,0,0,0,,believe it or not, I'm not the biggest fan of.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.21,0:00:15.95,EN,,0,0,0,,But that's just kind of how it is at this point.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.97,0:00:17.48,EN,,0,0,0,,If you wanna learn about redstone,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.50,0:00:19.30,EN,,0,0,0,,either you defeat an ancient city,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.32,0:00:20.36,EN,,0,0,0,,find a jungle temple,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.39,0:00:22.60,EN,,0,0,0,,or you type "redstone minecraft" into Google.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.63,0:00:23.99,EN,,0,0,0,,Which one would you choose?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.01,0:00:25.63,EN,,0,0,0,,I think I'll call this the wiki problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.65,0:00:27.16,EN,,0,0,0,,That's a story for another time though.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.19,0:00:29.92,EN,,0,0,0,,What we're interested in today are the results of that search.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.94,0:00:32.09,EN,,0,0,0,,The top ones are on a website called Fandom,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.12,0:00:33.44,EN,,0,0,0,,and they're both… terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:35.58,EN,,0,0,0,,There's instantly a pop-up asking for my age,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.60,0:00:38.72,EN,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure why the Minecraft wiki is so concerned about that kind of thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.75,0:00:39.60,EN,,0,0,0,,but whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.62,0:00:43.23,EN,,0,0,0,,The uses section reads like someone just listed everything redstone can do
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.25,0:00:45.52,EN,,0,0,0,,off the top of their head and called it a day
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.55,0:00:49.65,EN,,0,0,0,,On the side there's a bunch of suggestions for random pages, like the "Wither Storm".
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.68,0:00:52.54,EN,,0,0,0,,Uhh, yeah, I'm pretty sure that's only in Patton Oswalt edition.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.56,0:00:55.58,EN,,0,0,0,,And I bet you've noticed by now that it looks like we're getting 15 million merits,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.61,0:00:57.50,EN,,0,0,0,,because there's a video ad at the top,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.52,0:00:58.83,EN,,0,0,0,,banner ads on the sides,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.85,0:01:00.25,EN,,0,0,0,,and a video ad in the corner,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.27,0:01:03.27,EN,,0,0,0,,with only a sliver of the information that I actually need.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.30,0:01:04.53,EN,,0,0,0,,If we go to the second result—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.56,0:01:05.95,EN,,0,0,0,,I'm a kid now, trust me bro—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.98,0:01:06.95,EN,,0,0,0,,it's more of the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.98,0:01:09.35,EN,,0,0,0,,There are somehow even more ads than last time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.37,0:01:10.92,EN,,0,0,0,,This one has a lot more information
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.95,0:01:13.64,EN,,0,0,0,,but still doesn't have the crafter in the list of recipes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.67,0:01:16.25,EN,,0,0,0,,And the copper bulb is… just a question mark?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.28,0:01:19.12,EN,,0,0,0,,Y'know, maybe this is like, just a fan wiki or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.15,0:01:21.39,EN,,0,0,0,,It is on a website called Fandom, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.41,0:01:24.65,EN,,0,0,0,,Let's click on the wiki link on this random guy back in 2009.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.68,0:01:25.94,EN,,0,0,0,,This should take us to the real w—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.40,0:01:27.23,EN,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.26,0:01:28.61,EN,,0,0,0,,It takes us back to Fandom.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.63,0:01:29.68,EN,,0,0,0,,This is the real one.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.70,0:01:32.18,EN,,0,0,0,,And that's such a shame, because this is awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.20,0:01:35.28,EN,,0,0,0,,I remember back in the day that the wiki used to actually look professional.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.30,0:01:37.16,EN,,0,0,0,,How did the wiki go from looking like this
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.18,0:01:38.02,EN,,0,0,0,,to this?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.04,0:01:40.59,EN,,0,0,0,,How did it end up in the hands of a company like Fandom,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.61,0:01:42.87,EN,,0,0,0,,a huge corporation that everybody hates
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.90,0:01:44.55,EN,,0,0,0,,because of their constant urge to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.58,0:01:47.74,EN,,0,0,0,,suck out as much money from its users as physically possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.77,0:01:50.55,EN,,0,0,0,,And how has the wiki actually been getting way better recently…?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.58,0:01:54.55,EN,,0,0,0,,To find out, let's go over to the wiki from back in 2009.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.48,0:02:16.58,EN,,0,0,0,,The story starts with the Mojang forum.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.61,0:02:18.57,EN,,0,0,0,,They had just recently just made a little block game
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.60,0:02:20.14,EN,,0,0,0,,that was starting to get kinda popular,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.17,0:02:23.81,EN,,0,0,0,,and the forum was not equipped to deal with such large swaths of people.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.83,0:02:26.81,EN,,0,0,0,,So user CitricSquid—at 17 years old—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.84,0:02:28.89,EN,,0,0,0,,started up an unofficial Minecraft forum.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.92,0:02:31.12,EN,,0,0,0,,The guy who made the block game said that it was, quote,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.14,0:02:33.35,EN,,0,0,0,,"muuch better" than the official forum
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.37,0:02:35.75,EN,,0,0,0,,and eventually closed the one on mojang.com.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.77,0:02:37.99,EN,,0,0,0,,User Quatroking suggested to CitricSquid
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.01,0:02:41.68,EN,,0,0,0,,that a Minecraft wiki would be super useful to go along with the forums.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.71,0:02:44.80,EN,,0,0,0,,Citric agreed. So on June 17th, 2009,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.82,0:02:46.84,EN,,0,0,0,,He registered minecraftwiki.net,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.86,0:02:48.20,EN,,0,0,0,,set up MediaWiki on it—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.23,0:02:51.11,EN,,0,0,0,,the software that basically every wiki on earth uses—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.13,0:02:53.07,EN,,0,0,0,,and put Quatro in charge of moderating it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.09,0:02:56.05,EN,,0,0,0,,Mojang would eventually link to these pages on minecraft.net,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.08,0:02:58.93,EN,,0,0,0,,making them the all-but-official websites for the community.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.96,0:03:02.01,EN,,0,0,0,,At the beginning, the wiki actually wasn't very useful at all,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.04,0:03:03.83,EN,,0,0,0,,because the game was still very barebones—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.86,0:03:06.96,EN,,0,0,0,,there's only so much you can learn about a piece of stone back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.99,0:03:08.98,EN,,0,0,0,,That was, until crafting was added.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.01,0:03:11.39,EN,,0,0,0,,Recipes were not viewable in game, so you
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.42,0:03:13.90,EN,,0,0,0,,basically needed the wiki to play survival mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.93,0:03:16.00,EN,,0,0,0,,This meant that the popularity of the wiki was now
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.03,0:03:18.30,EN,,0,0,0,,basically tied to the success of the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.32,0:03:21.26,EN,,0,0,0,,And, uh, Minecraft was… kind of successful.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.29,0:03:22.79,EN,,0,0,0,,The more people visiting the website,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.81,0:03:25.33,EN,,0,0,0,,the more money CitricSquid had to spend on servers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.35,0:03:29.13,EN,,0,0,0,,It was so much that he actually ran out of money to rent them multiple times.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.16,0:03:31.22,EN,,0,0,0,,He got some financial help from aera—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.24,0:03:34.00,EN,,0,0,0,,who made the first Minecraft server with multiple worlds, by the way—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.02,0:03:36.74,EN,,0,0,0,,but the wiki was still growing extremely fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.76,0:03:40.57,EN,,0,0,0,,There was a point in 2010 where the average visitors to the site was doubling
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.60,0:03:43.15,EN,,0,0,0,,every single week for two months straight.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.17,0:03:46.92,EN,,0,0,0,,Citric later said that it cost tens of thousands of dollars a month
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.95,0:03:48.60,EN,,0,0,0,,to keep both websites running.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.63,0:03:53.01,EN,,0,0,0,,They had a big donation drive at one point which raised about $3500.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.04,0:03:54.74,EN,,0,0,0,,Since it was starting to get kinda sketchy
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.76,0:03:57.31,EN,,0,0,0,,and they really didn't want to beg people for money again,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.33,0:03:59.98,EN,,0,0,0,,he had to add an ad, which was a tad sad,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.01,0:04:01.19,EN,,0,0,0,,but that was all they had.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.22,0:04:04.67,EN,,0,0,0,,Because of the ad-generated revenue, they also registered a company
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.69,0:04:07.43,EN,,0,0,0,,called Redstone Wire Ltd to manage that revenue.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.45,0:04:09.87,EN,,0,0,0,,At this point, stresses were, uh, really high.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.90,0:04:12.70,EN,,0,0,0,,—"we were still suffering from fast rising traffic and costs,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.72,0:04:14.28,EN,,0,0,0,,things that we couldn't keep up with."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.30,0:04:16.62,EN,,0,0,0,,"WedTM, aera and myself (all volunteers)
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.65,0:04:19.82,EN,,0,0,0,,were the only people involved with the day to day operations,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.85,0:04:21.95,EN,,0,0,0,,WedTM with a full job of his own
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.97,0:04:25.79,EN,,0,0,0,,and aera with a business to run and myself with technical incompetence,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.82,0:04:29.34,EN,,0,0,0,,3 volunteers running sites that were now bigger than Stackoverflow."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.37,0:04:33.66,EN,,0,0,0,,—Can you imagine the pressure of hosting something so essential to this game?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.69,0:04:35.46,EN,,0,0,0,,Who knows how long they can keep this up!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.49,0:04:37.15,EN,,0,0,0,,If the game gets even more popular, then
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.18,0:04:38.77,EN,,0,0,0,,What the hell are they gonna do—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.79,0:04:39.70,EN,,0,0,0,,Uh—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.96,0:04:47.80,EN,,0,0,0,,Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.65,0:04:52.46,EN,,0,0,0,,You want to buy the wiki and the forum??
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.48,0:04:54.49,EN,,0,0,0,,Two months after Redstone Wire was founded,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.52,0:04:58.89,EN,,0,0,0,,they were contacted by Donovan Duncan, content director at Curse LLC.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.91,0:05:01.25,EN,,0,0,0,,At the time, Curse's big competitor, Wikia,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.28,0:05:04.39,EN,,0,0,0,,was making some very… anti-consumer decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.42,0:05:06.78,EN,,0,0,0,,They had just forced every single wiki on their site
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.81,0:05:08.79,EN,,0,0,0,,to switch their skin from this…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.82,0:05:10.12,EN,,0,0,0,,to this:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.20,0:05:13.27,EN,,0,0,0,,It's got locked width, way less customization,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.29,0:05:14.89,EN,,0,0,0,,a bunch of bullshit you don't care about,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.91,0:05:17.79,EN,,0,0,0,,and overall, it felt like Wikia was trying to drag you away
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.82,0:05:19.60,EN,,0,0,0,,from the actual wiki that you're looking at.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.63,0:05:22.22,EN,,0,0,0,,Nobody asked for this. Nothing was broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.25,0:05:23.86,EN,,0,0,0,,But they fixed it anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.88,0:05:25.64,EN,,0,0,0,,And by it, heh heh…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.67,0:05:26.73,EN,,0,0,0,,I mean the width.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.75,0:05:28.60,EN,,0,0,0,,Shortly after Oasis was revealed,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.62,0:05:31.18,EN,,0,0,0,,the extremely large World of Warcraft wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.21,0:05:34.72,EN,,0,0,0,,was looking to leave, and they decided to go over to Curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.75,0:05:37.37,EN,,0,0,0,,With this victory, Curse was ready to make some money moves,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.40,0:05:41.14,EN,,0,0,0,,one of which was to make absolutely sure that the huge Minecraft wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.16,0:05:43.90,EN,,0,0,0,,wouldn't go over to Wikia during its financial troubles.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.93,0:05:47.46,EN,,0,0,0,,Donovan would offer to buy the wiki and the forum from Redstone Wire
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.48,0:05:50.59,EN,,0,0,0,,and hire all three members of the company to work at Curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.62,0:05:52.88,EN,,0,0,0,,The big company would take care of running the backend,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.90,0:05:55.80,EN,,0,0,0,,and the Redstone Wire employees could focus on the community.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.82,0:05:59.32,EN,,0,0,0,,So the choice for Citric was either to keep going on this independent path,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.34,0:06:00.73,EN,,0,0,0,,with no clear way forward,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.75,0:06:03.09,EN,,0,0,0,,not knowing if the wiki would still exist for the next month,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.11,0:06:05.90,EN,,0,0,0,,not knowing if the game would grow more over the next couple of years—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.93,0:06:07.32,EN,,0,0,0,,uh, spoiler, it would—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.35,0:06:11.17,EN,,0,0,0,,and overall, just keep a ton of pressure on the shoulders of this 18-year-old kid
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.19,0:06:12.03,EN,,0,0,0,,or…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.37,0:06:13.98,EN,,0,0,0,,they could just say yes to Donovan.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.00,0:06:15.36,EN,,0,0,0,,Which one would you choose?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.38,0:06:17.15,EN,,0,0,0,,I think I'll call this the Donovan problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.92,0:06:20.88,EN,,0,0,0,,Needless to say, the deal went through.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.91,0:06:23.60,EN,,0,0,0,,Curse LLC was now the owner of the wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.62,0:06:27.11,EN,,0,0,0,,Redstone Wire Ltd would permanently dissolve less than a year later.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.13,0:06:29.52,EN,,0,0,0,,Makes sense, since the only websites they owned after that
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.54,0:06:33.01,EN,,0,0,0,,were minecraftmuseum.net and minecraftservers.com,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.04,0:06:34.92,EN,,0,0,0,,two websites that I've not even heard of.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.95,0:06:35.84,EN,,0,0,0,,For the next two years,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.87,0:06:38.87,EN,,0,0,0,,Curse would own and operate the Minecraft wiki basically like normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.89,0:06:42.31,EN,,0,0,0,,Some of the moderators were swapped around, some small things were changed,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.34,0:06:44.57,EN,,0,0,0,,but from the outside, nothing really happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.60,0:06:46.21,EN,,0,0,0,,The only evidence of Curse's involvement
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.23,0:06:49.08,EN,,0,0,0,,was at the bottom here with their little standard Curse footer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.11,0:06:50.26,EN,,0,0,0,,One thing Curse did do
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.29,0:06:51.83,EN,,0,0,0,,was sign a deal with Mojang,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.85,0:06:53.80,EN,,0,0,0,,making the wiki officially official.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.82,0:06:55.29,EN,,0,0,0,,In practical terms, this just means that
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.32,0:06:58.45,EN,,0,0,0,,Mojang could now list it on the website as the official wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.47,0:07:01.67,EN,,0,0,0,,and a year later, they changed the header on the Minecraft wiki as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.69,0:07:04.75,EN,,0,0,0,,From "the ultimate source on information about Minecraft"
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.77,0:07:07.95,EN,,0,0,0,,to "the official resource on information about Minecraft."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.97,0:07:11.73,EN,,0,0,0,,Wow, one and a half words. Incredible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.75,0:07:14.28,EN,,0,0,0,,The point is that this was some ethical usage of the wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.31,0:07:18.02,EN,,0,0,0,,I really respect them for not changing it very much and working to make it official.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.04,0:07:20.54,EN,,0,0,0,,Curse would acquire a bunch of other wikis in this time too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.57,0:07:22.39,EN,,0,0,0,,By September of 2012,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.41,0:07:23.66,EN,,0,0,0,,they were hosting 26 wikis
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.69,0:07:26.32,EN,,0,0,0,,for games like 2D Minecraft, medieval Minecraft,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.35,0:07:29.62,EN,,0,0,0,,radioactive Minecraft, and not-as-popular-as Minecraft.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.64,0:07:31.83,EN,,0,0,0,,They had a ton of very big wikis under their belt,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.85,0:07:33.72,EN,,0,0,0,,and they wanted to grow it even more.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.75,0:07:37.09,EN,,0,0,0,,However, it was getting pretty hard to keep doing that with their hands-on approach.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.12,0:07:40.41,EN,,0,0,0,,Each wiki acquisition seemed like a very personal task,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.44,0:07:42.01,EN,,0,0,0,,and they can't do that forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.04,0:07:46.06,EN,,0,0,0,,If they wanted to compete with a company like Wikia, something was going to have to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.08,0:07:48.48,EN,,0,0,0,,So in 2012, Curse came out with Hydra,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.50,0:07:50.88,EN,,0,0,0,,a custom build of the MediaWiki software
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.90,0:07:54.31,EN,,0,0,0,,which was designed to host a bunch of wikis with only one base.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.33,0:07:55.74,EN,,0,0,0,,Oh, I see why they called it that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.77,0:07:58.47,EN,,0,0,0,,They wouldn't have to update each wiki individually anymore,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.49,0:08:02.29,EN,,0,0,0,,and instead update one server running Hydra and call it a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.32,0:08:04.70,EN,,0,0,0,,This made each wiki way less personal to deal with
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.73,0:08:07.52,EN,,0,0,0,,So they could have a lot more wikis if they wanted to.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.55,0:08:09.82,EN,,0,0,0,,Because of this revelation, they put Hydra into
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.84,0:08:12.48,EN,,0,0,0,,their own wiki-hosting service called Gamepedia.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.50,0:08:16.10,EN,,0,0,0,,You could go to gamepedia.com and suggest a wiki to exist
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.12,0:08:19.48,EN,,0,0,0,,and if they got enough suggestions and a lot of possible staff members
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.50,0:08:21.66,EN,,0,0,0,,and the employees at Curse personally liked it
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.68,0:08:24.81,EN,,0,0,0,,and you guessed the number of jellybeans in this magic jar,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.83,0:08:25.81,EN,,0,0,0,,they would make it happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.83,0:08:30.36,EN,,0,0,0,,they would all be hosted on gamepedia.com with a subdomain of which game it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.38,0:08:33.49,EN,,0,0,0,,So in September of 2013, the Minecraft wiki was now hosted
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.52,0:08:37.61,EN,,0,0,0,,on the much clunkier URL of minecraft.gamepedia.com.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.63,0:08:39.55,EN,,0,0,0,,It was even worse if you didn't speak English
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.57,0:08:41.56,EN,,0,0,0,,because the link would include the language in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.59,0:08:45.84,EN,,0,0,0,,So Germans would have to go to minecraft-de.gamepedia.com.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.86,0:08:47.78,EN,,0,0,0,,For reference, here's my credit card number.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.81,0:08:49.28,EN,,0,0,0,,Even though it was on a new website,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.30,0:08:50.93,EN,,0,0,0,,all of the old links would still work
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.96,0:08:53.69,EN,,0,0,0,,but they would redirect to the relevant page on Gamepedia.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.71,0:08:54.81,EN,,0,0,0,,Okay, so for recap:
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.84,0:08:58.73,EN,,0,0,0,,Gamepedia is the name of the hosting service for all of the Gamepedia wikis,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.76,0:09:01.83,EN,,0,0,0,,which uses Hydra as its custom build of MediaWiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.86,0:09:04.84,EN,,0,0,0,,All of the wikis are hosted on Gamepedia, the website,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.86,0:09:08.46,EN,,0,0,0,,and also Gamepedia is a department inside of Curse Media,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.49,0:09:12.10,EN,,0,0,0,,which is a department inside of the overall company of Curse LLC.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.13,0:09:13.19,EN,,0,0,0,,It's really quite simple!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.21,0:09:15.75,EN,,0,0,0,,Curse Media also had departments like the Curse Network
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.77,0:09:17.41,EN,,0,0,0,,Which ran the forums for many games,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.43,0:09:19.01,EN,,0,0,0,,including the Minecraft forum,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.04,0:09:20.50,EN,,0,0,0,,and also Curse Entertainment,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.53,0:09:21.74,EN,,0,0,0,,which covered live events,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.77,0:09:24.50,EN,,0,0,0,,and some other insane stuff that I'll put in this footnote.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.52,0:09:26.53,EN,,0,0,0,,Hydra came out in September of 2012,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.55,0:09:28.30,EN,,0,0,0,,and in eight months they were hosting
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.33,0:09:31.03,EN,,0,0,0,,ten times the amount of wikis that they had before.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.06,0:09:33.45,EN,,0,0,0,,This meant that Gamepedia wasn't just a wiki hoster
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.47,0:09:36.10,EN,,0,0,0,,they practically had a whole farm full of wikis,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.12,0:09:40.01,EN,,0,0,0,,which is why anytime a bunch of wikis are together in one place it's called a wiki farm.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.04,0:09:41.77,EN,,0,0,0,,Unless it's a wiki zoo, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.80,0:09:43.54,EN,,0,0,0,,This isn't bad, per se,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.57,0:09:47.97,EN,,0,0,0,,but now the Minecraft wiki is suddenly a small part of a huge wiki farm.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.99,0:09:51.15,EN,,0,0,0,,Even though it was the most popular wiki on Gamepedia,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.18,0:09:53.82,EN,,0,0,0,,it was still one out of hundreds of wikis.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.85,0:09:56.37,EN,,0,0,0,,Only so much care and attention can go around.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.39,0:09:59.02,EN,,0,0,0,,The Minecraft wiki was officially moved over to Gamepedia
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.05,0:10:01.59,EN,,0,0,0,,on Thursday, September 19th, 2013,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.61,0:10:04.15,EN,,0,0,0,,directly after Minecraft's peak popularity.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.18,0:10:07.08,EN,,0,0,0,,So most people remember the wiki looking… kinda like this,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.11,0:10:10.01,EN,,0,0,0,,either owned by Curse, or already on Gamepedia.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.03,0:10:13.94,EN,,0,0,0,,Curse was one of the most professional video game companies on the internet at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.94,0:10:17.62,EN,,0,0,0,,They had a multi-channel network, a TeamSpeak competitor, an esports team…
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.65,0:10:20.24,EN,,0,0,0,,You know those old mcspotlight videos? They made those.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.26,0:10:23.22,EN,,0,0,0,,And they still operate CurseForge for modding to this day,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.24,0:10:25.84,EN,,0,0,0,,through their current corporate overlord, Overwolf.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.86,0:10:30.10,EN,,0,0,0,,And Curse, for the most part, was doing pretty… kinda okay, I guess, at it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.13,0:10:33.56,EN,,0,0,0,,There was some stuff about Bukkit, which is a story for another time…
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.58,0:10:37.81,EN,,0,0,0,,They have this gigantic right sidebar just to show tweets from Mojang for some reason…
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.84,0:10:39.86,EN,,0,0,0,,It took them two years to remove that, by the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.88,0:10:43.57,EN,,0,0,0,,Most of us were kids at the time, though, and I know that I never noticed any of that stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.59,0:10:45.97,EN,,0,0,0,,I just used the wiki and didn't really think twice about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.99,0:10:48.29,EN,,0,0,0,,They were able to do basically everything on the internet,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.31,0:10:50.28,EN,,0,0,0,,and I felt like they were pretty trustworthy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.31,0:10:52.91,EN,,0,0,0,,It almost seems like they were just the classic fast-growing tech company
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.94,0:10:55.55,EN,,0,0,0,,which was able to make people love them by just burning tons of money
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.58,0:10:59.19,EN,,0,0,0,,in hopes that a big corporation would buy them out of the massive debt that they're in
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.21,0:11:01.91,EN,,0,0,0,,and teach them how to make money while burning all their goodwill
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.94,0:11:06.26,EN,,0,0,0,,and the founder gets to go into retirement and become an angel investor at the age of 36.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.84,0:11:10.22,EN,,0,0,0,,And that's exactly what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.24,0:11:15.01,EN,,0,0,0,,In 2016, there was this small mom-and-pop company called Twitch Interactive, Inc.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.04,0:11:16.11,EN,,0,0,0,,owned by Amazon
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.13,0:11:19.50,EN,,0,0,0,,and they would buy Curse LLC and all of its subsidiaries.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.53,0:11:24.29,EN,,0,0,0,,So now, Jeffrey pissbottle Bezos owns the Minecraft wiki and the Minecraft forum.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.31,0:11:27.01,EN,,0,0,0,,Most people don't really remember this time in the Minecraft community,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.03,0:11:30.92,EN,,0,0,0,,because 2016 to 2018 was kind of the dark ages for Minecraft.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.95,0:11:33.62,EN,,0,0,0,,This was when a lot of the quantity mobs were being added
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.64,0:11:36.03,EN,,0,0,0,,with no reason to ever interact with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.06,0:11:38.49,EN,,0,0,0,,This is also when the knowledge book was added to the game,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.51,0:11:43.03,EN,,0,0,0,,which made the wiki's big role in providing crafting recipes now completely irrelevant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.06,0:11:46.25,EN,,0,0,0,,Being owned by Amazon wasn't actually that big of a deal for the wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.27,0:11:47.88,EN,,0,0,0,,They didn't really change much over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.90,0:11:49.69,EN,,0,0,0,,They messed up some fonts on the forums,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.71,0:11:53.44,EN,,0,0,0,,which would be really annoying if you were using old forum posts for a video or something—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.47,0:11:54.30,EN,,0,0,0,,who would do that…?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.33,0:11:58.31,EN,,0,0,0,,And they made all of the login systems across the website sync with Twitch, because…
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.34,0:11:59.18,EN,,0,0,0,,why not.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.20,0:12:01.32,EN,,0,0,0,,I assume that CitricSquid was forced at gunpoint
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.35,0:12:04.40,EN,,0,0,0,,to post this super cringy corporate press-release bullshit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.42,0:12:06.74,EN,,0,0,0,,"Get your PogChamp emote ready"?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.77,0:12:09.55,EN,,0,0,0,,"You're going to need it"? God damn, I'm so sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.58,0:12:11.92,EN,,0,0,0,,But overall, it wasn't terrible for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.95,0:12:15.42,EN,,0,0,0,,Twitch's main gig at the time was doing stuff with the Curse Client,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.45,0:12:16.63,EN,,0,0,0,,renamed Twitch App,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.65,0:12:21.27,EN,,0,0,0,,which if you ever used, you'll know was a hellspawn abomination from the very start.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.29,0:12:24.63,EN,,0,0,0,,They really wanted this to work, though, so the wiki was mostly spared.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.66,0:12:27.10,EN,,0,0,0,,The Twitch app lasted til 2022,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.13,0:12:29.26,EN,,0,0,0,,and then it was zapped from existence
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.28,0:12:31.90,EN,,0,0,0,,and they've scrubbed all mention of it from everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.93,0:12:33.94,EN,,0,0,0,,But I don't forget. I never forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.96,0:12:36.48,EN,,0,0,0,,Man, it's kinda weird that they didn't mess with the wiki, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.50,0:12:39.62,EN,,0,0,0,,I don't— I wonder if there was some sort of ulterior motive to this purcha—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.16,0:12:42.24,EN,,0,0,0,,Knock knock.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.26,0:12:44.03,EN,,0,0,0,,It's Fandom, Inc.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.06,0:12:45.39,EN,,0,0,0,,With huge vaults.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.41,0:12:46.44,EN,,0,0,0,,With money.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.47,0:12:47.65,EN,,0,0,0,,Money vaults.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.68,0:12:49.30,EN,,0,0,0,,Open your wallets.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.33,0:12:51.47,EN,,0,0,0,,Stop having them be closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.50,0:12:55.65,EN,,0,0,0,,In 2018, Fandom bought the entire Curse Media department from Twitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.68,0:12:58.08,EN,,0,0,0,,This meant that Curse was basically now split in two,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.11,0:13:00.56,EN,,0,0,0,,with the wikis and forums going over to Fandom,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.58,0:13:03.31,EN,,0,0,0,,while CurseForge and the Twitch app would stay at Twitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.34,0:13:06.72,EN,,0,0,0,,If you're wondering what the hell Fandom was doing this whole entire time, well—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.75,0:13:07.98,EN,,0,0,0,,surprise, surprise—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.00,0:13:11.07,EN,,0,0,0,,Fandom is just the new name for our old friend Wikia!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.09,0:13:14.50,EN,,0,0,0,,That's right, the company that made such anti-consumer decisions
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.53,0:13:17.30,EN,,0,0,0,,that Curse used that hatred to propel their own business!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.33,0:13:21.11,EN,,0,0,0,,The people that made a design so terrible that the biggest wiki that they owned
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.13,0:13:22.96,EN,,0,0,0,,left days after it was revealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.99,0:13:27.12,EN,,0,0,0,,The people who, just a year earlier, had implemented auto-playing video ads
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.14,0:13:30.42,EN,,0,0,0,,that were so obnoxious that they convinced the RuneScape wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.44,0:13:34.17,EN,,0,0,0,,to jump ship and pay for the wiki themselves rather than Fandom.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.20,0:13:38.79,EN,,0,0,0,,Those are the same people that just bought every single wiki on Gamepedia.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.73,0:13:40.71,EN,,0,0,0,,Yaaay.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.73,0:13:44.49,EN,,0,0,0,,I guess in the long run, Wikia eventually did get hold of the Minecraft wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.52,0:13:45.70,EN,,0,0,0,,Well, wait a minute, wait a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.72,0:13:47.73,EN,,0,0,0,,How does a random company like Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.76,0:13:50.58,EN,,0,0,0,,just buy an entire department from Amazon?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.61,0:13:53.41,EN,,0,0,0,,They don't exactly just put it up on the website for Prime Day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.44,0:13:56.69,EN,,0,0,0,,Maybe Mr. Bezos was just feeling super generous that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.71,0:14:01.37,EN,,0,0,0,,Or maybe it's because Amazon invested a fuckton of money into Wikia in 2006.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.39,0:14:03.07,EN,,0,0,0,,How much money, we don't know for sure,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.09,0:14:06.41,EN,,0,0,0,,but Amazon says that they were the sole investor in Series B
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.43,0:14:10.57,EN,,0,0,0,,{\pos(976,914)}and according to Crunchbase, Wikia got ten million dollars in series B,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.60,0:14:13.57,EN,,0,0,0,,so I think that "fuckton" is a good ballpark.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.60,0:14:16.69,EN,,0,0,0,,It's great to know that Fandom and Amazon are great friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.71,0:14:20.31,EN,,0,0,0,,That's just… that's just awesome. Y'know, they're just best buds, y'know? They're just…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.33,0:14:22.19,EN,,0,0,0,,They're just out here, facing the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.21,0:14:23.33,EN,,0,0,0,,They're just going together,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.35,0:14:24.89,EN,,0,0,0,,They're soulmates, they love each other,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.92,0:14:26.58,EN,,0,0,0,,they're kissing, they're hugging, they're cuddling.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.61,0:14:27.58,EN,,0,0,0,,We love to see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.61,0:14:30.96,EN,,0,0,0,,Very coincidentally, just a couple months before this purchase,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.99,0:14:33.87,EN,,0,0,0,,Fandom was acquired by Integrated Media Company,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.90,0:14:38.36,EN,,0,0,0,,which is a company inside of the Texas Pacific Group, a private equity firm.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.39,0:14:41.76,EN,,0,0,0,,If you don't know what the hell private equity is and why it's so firm
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.79,0:14:44.14,EN,,0,0,0,,well, neither did I before making this video.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.17,0:14:46.81,EN,,0,0,0,,Basically, it's like House Flipper but for millionaires.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.84,0:14:51.09,EN,,0,0,0,,A bunch of rich assholes form Ultron in order to take out a loan
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.12,0:14:54.20,EN,,0,0,0,,and buy a Silicon Valley company that doesn't know how to make money
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.23,0:14:57.12,EN,,0,0,0,,then they desperately try to increase that company's value
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.15,0:14:59.69,EN,,0,0,0,,as fast as possible to pay back the loan.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.72,0:15:02.71,EN,,0,0,0,,And at the end of it, the firm doesn't owe any money to the bank,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.74,0:15:04.81,EN,,0,0,0,,and now they own a huge tech company.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.83,0:15:09.25,EN,,0,0,0,,The rich asshole at the rich-asshole helm in buying Fandom was Jonathan Miller,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.27,0:15:13.29,EN,,0,0,0,,who worked at such fun-loving companies as Viacom, and News Corporation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.31,0:15:15.45,EN,,0,0,0,,If you wanted to know what his business strategy is,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.48,0:15:20.02,EN,,0,0,0,,In 2004, he spent hundreds of millions of dollars at AOL
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.05,0:15:23.77,EN,,0,0,0,,to buy a website called advertising.com.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.80,0:15:25.29,EN,,0,0,0,,advertising
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.32,0:15:26.70,EN,,0,0,0,,dot com.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.72,0:15:30.01,EN,,0,0,0,,The writing was on the wall the whole time, guys, Jesus Christ.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.03,0:15:32.57,EN,,0,0,0,,Basically, if you thought that Amazon wanted money,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.59,0:15:37.36,EN,,0,0,0,,These guys are even worse. And they now control every Gamepedia wiki in existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.38,0:15:39.35,EN,,0,0,0,,TPG has partnered with a lot of…
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.37,0:15:41.37,EN,,0,0,0,,great, amazing brands in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.39,0:15:43.93,EN,,0,0,0,,Like Ellucian—all college kids just shuddered—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.96,0:15:46.41,EN,,0,0,0,,Airbnb, Uber, Toast credit card,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.43,0:15:47.96,EN,,0,0,0,,and fucking Burger King?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.99,0:15:51.33,EN,,0,0,0,,They're the progenitors of such great ideas as… the Whopper Bar.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.35,0:15:53.89,EN,,0,0,0,,According to the president of marketing, they are…
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.91,0:15:56.57,EN,,0,0,0,,like Pimp My Ride but for burgers??
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.59,0:15:57.82,EN,,0,0,0,,Shut the fuck up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.85,0:16:00.36,EN,,0,0,0,,Hey burgerista, can you pimp my Whopper
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.39,0:16:02.79,EN,,0,0,0,,with some extra guacamole please?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.81,0:16:04.10,EN,,0,0,0,,Thank you! Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.13,0:16:05.15,EN,,0,0,0,,…What were we talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.18,0:16:06.02,EN,,0,0,0,,Oh, right right right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.04,0:16:08.79,EN,,0,0,0,,While they bought the whole department of Curse Media from Twitch,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.82,0:16:11.45,EN,,0,0,0,,It seems like they were only really in it for the wikis.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.47,0:16:16.45,EN,,0,0,0,,The Minecraft forum was so starved for funds that just four months after this sale,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.48,0:16:19.08,EN,,0,0,0,,they announced the entire website was getting archived.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.11,0:16:22.66,EN,,0,0,0,,In response, Mojang removed the "woo, minecraftforum!" splash text
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.69,0:16:24.28,EN,,0,0,0,,as it wouldn't make sense anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.31,0:16:26.55,EN,,0,0,0,,Just four days before it was about to be archived,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.58,0:16:28.83,EN,,0,0,0,,the Minecraft forum was sold to Magic Find,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.85,0:16:30.61,EN,,0,0,0,,which is still where it is today.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.63,0:16:33.79,EN,,0,0,0,,Very sadly, Mojang never re-added the splash text.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.82,0:16:39.03,EN,,0,0,0,,This would be the fate of many of the non-wiki properties bought by Fandom in late 2018,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.06,0:16:40.41,EN,,0,0,0,,either rotted to death,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.43,0:16:41.98,EN,,0,0,0,,or sold to another company.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.01,0:16:44.55,EN,,0,0,0,,This is very standard private equity type stuff,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.58,0:16:47.79,EN,,0,0,0,,if it's losing them a single cent of money it's gonezo.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.82,0:16:49.97,EN,,0,0,0,,I mean, they've gotta pay the bank back somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.99,0:16:51.14,EN,,0,0,0,,For the actual wikis though,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.16,0:16:53.12,EN,,0,0,0,,they wanted to keep those around.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.14,0:16:54.85,EN,,0,0,0,,The sale happened in late 2018
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.88,0:16:58.40,EN,,0,0,0,,and all of the Gamepedia wikis would stay on their old websites for awhile.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.42,0:16:59.40,EN,,0,0,0,,Over the next two years,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.43,0:17:01.89,EN,,0,0,0,,they would slowly merge all the wikis together
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.92,0:17:05.29,EN,,0,0,0,,And this came to a culmination on November 4th 2021,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.31,0:17:09.05,EN,,0,0,0,,when Fandom announced that all Gamepedia and Fandom wikis on the desktop
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.08,0:17:10.49,EN,,0,0,0,,were getting forcibly merged,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.52,0:17:11.77,EN,,0,0,0,,whether they liked it or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.80,0:17:15.88,EN,,0,0,0,,As we covered earlier, Wikia—Fandom— already had a ton of wikis on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.91,0:17:20.31,EN,,0,0,0,,This included an alternative Minecraft wiki on minecraft.fandom.com.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.33,0:17:22.11,EN,,0,0,0,,So, which one was the real one?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.14,0:17:23.69,EN,,0,0,0,,Well, the Gamepedia one was,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.72,0:17:25.84,EN,,0,0,0,,because it was actually officially official.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.86,0:17:28.90,EN,,0,0,0,,And since it was the more updated and recognized one too,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.93,0:17:32.52,EN,,0,0,0,,the Fandom wiki had to just kind of suck it up and join the Gamepedia wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.54,0:17:38.05,EN,,0,0,0,,The old Fandom wiki would be archived and moved to minecraft-archive.fandom.com,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.07,0:17:41.71,EN,,0,0,0,,and the Gamepedia wiki would be moved to minecraft.fandom.com,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.73,0:17:43.62,EN,,0,0,0,,becoming the new Fandom wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.64,0:17:47.57,EN,,0,0,0,,Any links to minecraftwiki.net or minecraft.gamepedia.com
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.59,0:17:52.69,EN,,0,0,0,,or minecraft.wikia.com would redirect to the relevant page on the new Fandom wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.72,0:17:55.41,EN,,0,0,0,,And these are the two search results that we saw in the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.43,0:17:58.55,EN,,0,0,0,,And, uh, wow. Isn't this just beautiful?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.57,0:18:00.67,EN,,0,0,0,,Wow. It's just, like— It's stunning.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.22,0:18:02.21,EN,,0,0,0,,Like a stun gun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.23,0:18:03.72,EN,,0,0,0,,I mean, look at this fuckin' website.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.75,0:18:06.24,EN,,0,0,0,,It's basically Pimp My Ride but for advertisements.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.26,0:18:07.38,EN,,0,0,0,,The website is slow,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.41,0:18:10.31,EN,,0,0,0,,There are dumbass quizzes and tabs and sidebars
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.34,0:18:13.60,EN,,0,0,0,,and video ads and recommended pages and a bunch of other more shit
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.63,0:18:16.95,EN,,0,0,0,,trying to steal your attention away from what's actually on the wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.97,0:18:19.83,EN,,0,0,0,,And overall, just looking at this thing just makes me sad, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.86,0:18:22.87,EN,,0,0,0,,The wiki is supposed to be about giving information to the public.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.90,0:18:25.71,EN,,0,0,0,,It's supposed to be an online encyclopedia.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.74,0:18:29.69,EN,,0,0,0,,Imagine you open up an encyclopedia and right where the information you want is,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.72,0:18:31.59,EN,,0,0,0,,you see a big fucking ad.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.62,0:18:35.63,EN,,0,0,0,,I think that it's important that information remains free and accessible to everyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.65,0:18:38.99,EN,,0,0,0,,and a company like Fandom completely flies in the face of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.02,0:18:42.59,EN,,0,0,0,,And while yes, Fandom does make creating a wiki more accessible,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.61,0:18:45.15,EN,,0,0,0,,Their actions are repeatedly going in the direction of
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.18,0:18:48.53,EN,,0,0,0,,making the actual information on the wiki less accessible
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.56,0:18:49.73,EN,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's just me
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.75,0:18:53.04,EN,,0,0,0,,but I don't think that Fandom is out here trying to make the world better.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.07,0:18:55.60,EN,,0,0,0,,They're not trying to improve upon the wiki format.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.63,0:18:58.64,EN,,0,0,0,,They're a for-profit company owned by a private equity firm.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.66,0:19:02.03,EN,,0,0,0,,I think, maybe, guys, they're trying to make money. I'm not sure, though,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.05,0:19:04.11,EN,,0,0,0,,this taxi does look pretty normal to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.13,0:19:06.88,EN,,0,0,0,,I want to say that I understand that all wikis can't be this
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.90,0:19:09.89,EN,,0,0,0,,perfect, no-ad utopia like Wikipedia is,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.92,0:19:12.78,EN,,0,0,0,,but you can sustainably run a wiki on ads
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.80,0:19:15.31,EN,,0,0,0,,and not have it look like this, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.34,0:19:16.74,EN,,0,0,0,,There's a point where the ads go from
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.76,0:19:19.38,EN,,0,0,0,,"oh, we're just doing this to support the server costs"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.40,0:19:21.71,EN,,0,0,0,,to "we're doing this because we want money"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.74,0:19:24.69,EN,,0,0,0,,and I think Fandom has far surpassed that point.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.72,0:19:28.28,EN,,0,0,0,,I mean, profitability was basically the pitch when Fandom was started.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.30,0:19:32.36,EN,,0,0,0,,Jimmy Wales, the one and only founder of Wikipedia (definitely trust me bro),
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.39,0:19:35.19,EN,,0,0,0,,was sitting around in the dense jungle surrounding his house
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.21,0:19:36.12,EN,,0,0,0,,and asked himself
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.14,0:19:38.45,EN,,0,0,0,,"what if I can make money off of this?"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.48,0:19:40.90,EN,,0,0,0,,The answer was probably "that would be shit".
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.18,0:19:44.98,EN,,0,0,0,,And so Wikicities was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.00,0:19:46.68,EN,,0,0,0,,It was a play off GeoCities.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.71,0:19:51.11,EN,,0,0,0,,GeoCities allowed people with very little coding experience to start their own website,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.14,0:19:54.49,EN,,0,0,0,,and in the same way, Wikicities would help people start their own wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.52,0:19:58.34,EN,,0,0,0,,They were born in the era where people still knew what the hell GeoCities was,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.37,0:19:59.95,EN,,0,0,0,,and are still around today,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.97,0:20:03.79,EN,,0,0,0,,slowly but surely turning the internet into an increasingly locked-down place.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.82,0:20:05.93,EN,,0,0,0,,Not a place where anyone can be themselves,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.96,0:20:08.94,EN,,0,0,0,,but a place where only large corporations can be themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.97,0:20:11.09,EN,,0,0,0,,The wiki represents the idyllic internet
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.12,0:20:14.61,EN,,0,0,0,,of hope and free information and connection and independence
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.64,0:20:17.78,EN,,0,0,0,,and Fandom represents the actual internet that we live in:
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.80,0:20:22.31,EN,,0,0,0,,one of large corporations, walled gardens, and a lot of advertisements.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.34,0:20:26.14,EN,,0,0,0,,And sometimes it can feel like we just have to kinda ride the wave,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.17,0:20:30.76,EN,,0,0,0,,take the beating, and continue to feel utterly powerless as a citizen of the internet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.68,0:20:33.36,EN,,0,0,0,,But luckily for us, though,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.38,0:20:35.36,EN,,0,0,0,,there is something we can do about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.55,0:20:41.87,EN,,0,0,0,,This wiki, minecraft.fandom.com,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.90,0:20:44.02,EN,,0,0,0,,is not technically the official wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.05,0:20:46.18,EN,,0,0,0,,There is no official wiki anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.21,0:20:49.30,EN,,0,0,0,,When it came time for Dremelmoth to renew the contract on that,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.33,0:20:52.66,EN,,0,0,0,,they instead said "fuck off" and gave them a huge list of demands.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.68,0:20:54.52,EN,,0,0,0,,I hope those one and a half words were worth it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.54,0:20:58.68,EN,,0,0,0,,If you want to draw a direct line from the original Minecraft wiki from 2009
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.70,0:21:00.19,EN,,0,0,0,,to this Fandom one, well,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.22,0:21:01.30,EN,,0,0,0,,that's what we've just done.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.32,0:21:04.46,EN,,0,0,0,,It's all the same wiki, it's just changed owners a million times.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.48,0:21:07.96,EN,,0,0,0,,That's why this link from 2009 still works to get you to the wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.99,0:21:10.34,EN,,0,0,0,,However, if we look at the search results from earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.36,0:21:12.77,EN,,0,0,0,,we actually see a mysterious third wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.79,0:21:16.13,EN,,0,0,0,,This one's on a completely different website, minecraft.wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.16,0:21:20.58,EN,,0,0,0,,It looks much more like Wikipedia, it's all up-to-date, and all of the recipes are there,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.61,0:21:24.35,EN,,0,0,0,,And, uh— I mean, holy shit! I mean, look at it! There's no ads!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.38,0:21:28.54,EN,,0,0,0,,The entire screen is not full of ads, this is crazy! I didn't know this was possible!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.56,0:21:30.78,EN,,0,0,0,,This one is so much better, what the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.80,0:21:32.38,EN,,0,0,0,,Why is this the third result?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.41,0:21:36.31,EN,,0,0,0,,Why does the Fandom wiki still exist when this one seems to be way better?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.34,0:21:39.74,EN,,0,0,0,,To understand that, we have to understand how wikis even work.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.76,0:21:43.31,EN,,0,0,0,,In this video, I've said a bunch of times that somebody "owns" the wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.34,0:21:45.70,EN,,0,0,0,,but what I really mean is that they own
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.73,0:21:49.81,EN,,0,0,0,,the responsibility to run the web servers that the wiki is hosted on.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.84,0:21:53.81,EN,,0,0,0,,They control the wiki branding, and they own the domain that it's hosted on.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.83,0:21:55.15,EN,,0,0,0,,Much to Fandom's chagrin,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.18,0:21:56.73,EN,,0,0,0,,you cannot purchase a fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.76,0:21:58.24,EN,,0,0,0,,What is actually on the wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.27,0:22:00.88,EN,,0,0,0,,in terms of text, is up to the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.91,0:22:03.73,EN,,0,0,0,,Because of this, the people on the Minecraft wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.76,0:22:07.30,EN,,0,0,0,,were starting to have some conversations about… maybe leaving Fandom.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.33,0:22:08.90,EN,,0,0,0,,And right when nobody expected him,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.92,0:22:10.05,EN,,0,0,0,,Grimace struck.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.07,0:22:11.52,EN,,0,0,0,,Yes, that one. I'm serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.55,0:22:13.40,EN,,0,0,0,,On June 14th, 2023,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.42,0:22:17.02,EN,,0,0,0,,Don's rizzed up Fandom with their level 3 gyatt and some Fanum tax
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.04,0:22:19.63,EN,,0,0,0,,to goon all over the McDonald's main skibidi page
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.66,0:22:22.08,EN,,0,0,0,,with a shillmaxxing advert for the Grimace shake.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.11,0:22:25.04,EN,,0,0,0,,The redpilled sigmas at the wiki were forced to gobble glizzies
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.07,0:22:28.89,EN,,0,0,0,,while the Shadow Wizard Money Gang was just putting ads in the bag the ocky way,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.91,0:22:32.17,EN,,0,0,0,,which made them very sus of they opps, losing them a ton of aura.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.20,0:22:33.06,EN,,0,0,0,,This was the final straw—
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.09,0:22:34.57,EN,,0,0,0,,If you understood what I just said,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.59,0:22:35.73,EN,,0,0,0,,please go outside today.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.75,0:22:37.65,EN,,0,0,0,,This was the final straw for a lot of people,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.67,0:22:39.95,EN,,0,0,0,,as it signified to every community on Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.98,0:22:42.60,EN,,0,0,0,,that there was now nothing left that was sacred to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.63,0:22:45.45,EN,,0,0,0,,Any part of the wiki, even a locked front page,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.48,0:22:49.27,EN,,0,0,0,,could now be forcibly changed into an advertisement with little notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.30,0:22:52.10,EN,,0,0,0,,While this was unlikely to happen to a game like Minecraft,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.13,0:22:54.14,EN,,0,0,0,,it's the precedent that was concerning.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.16,0:22:56.67,EN,,0,0,0,,Now, what even is the point of the wiki anymore?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.70,0:23:00.06,EN,,0,0,0,,The entire thing belongs to Fandom, they just changed it!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.09,0:23:01.96,EN,,0,0,0,,With the fuel of the Grimace incident,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.99,0:23:04.30,EN,,0,0,0,,people were even more willing to hear people out
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.32,0:23:05.83,EN,,0,0,0,,about ditching this fuckin' place.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.86,0:23:08.43,EN,,0,0,0,,This had already gotten a lot of traction in the Discord server,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.46,0:23:11.73,EN,,0,0,0,,and since they were actually being really serious this time,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.75,0:23:14.74,EN,,0,0,0,,they moved the conversation over to a discussion page on the wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.77,0:23:17.06,EN,,0,0,0,,for input from people who didn't use Discord.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.08,0:23:18.50,EN,,0,0,0,,It's time to get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.53,0:23:20.62,EN,,0,0,0,,…But, uhh, how do you do that, actually?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.64,0:23:22.96,EN,,0,0,0,,Believe it or not, Fandom actually has a whole page
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.98,0:23:24.86,EN,,0,0,0,,about how you can just pack up and leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.89,0:23:25.99,EN,,0,0,0,,It's called forking,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.01,0:23:27.55,EN,,0,0,0,,(because spooning was already taken)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.58,0:23:31.07,EN,,0,0,0,,and it's the process of starting a new version off of the base of the old one.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.09,0:23:32.18,EN,,0,0,0,,However, when you fork,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.21,0:23:33.97,EN,,0,0,0,,they have three big rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.99,0:23:35.23,EN,,0,0,0,,You can't destroy the old wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.25,0:23:37.63,EN,,0,0,0,,you can't advertise the new wiki on the old one,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.66,0:23:39.91,EN,,0,0,0,,and the admins can only admin one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.94,0:23:42.28,EN,,0,0,0,,These are all things that make leaving Fandom way harder,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.30,0:23:45.05,EN,,0,0,0,,as the old Fandom wiki has to still exist
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.08,0:23:47.48,EN,,0,0,0,,and compete with whatever new wiki you make.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.50,0:23:51.68,EN,,0,0,0,,These rules are kind of just the natural thing that people would do if it was an actual fork,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.71,0:23:53.99,EN,,0,0,0,,where both wikis are actively in development.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.02,0:23:57.65,EN,,0,0,0,,But if you want to move the whole wiki off of Fandom, they make that hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.67,0:24:00.33,EN,,0,0,0,,And then at the bottom of the page they have a final plea to
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.35,0:24:03.28,EN,,0,0,0,,"Oh, pwease, pwease stay on Fandom though!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.31,0:24:06.17,EN,,0,0,0,,It's weally weally hawd to weave…
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.20,0:24:07.60,EN,,0,0,0,,Because we say so…"
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.62,0:24:09.05,EN,,0,0,0,,So, a referendum was opened.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.08,0:24:13.88,EN,,0,0,0,,Basically, rank your top choices for forking, with staying on Fandom being an option too.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.91,0:24:17.60,EN,,0,0,0,,Now that this was actually serious, everyone could, um…
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.63,0:24:20.20,EN,,0,0,0,,express their real feelings about Fandom.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.22,0:24:22.87,EN,,0,0,0,,—"Fandom is terrible, and anything else would be an upgrade."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.90,0:24:25.45,EN,,0,0,0,,"The constant ads as well as the intrusive sidebar
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.48,0:24:27.79,EN,,0,0,0,,make it very annoying to use the site."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.81,0:24:29.92,EN,,0,0,0,,—"The wiki host is becoming less and less stable,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.94,0:24:32.12,EN,,0,0,0,,controversial innovations are being imposed,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.15,0:24:35.63,EN,,0,0,0,,and what has been broken for a long time is not updated or deleted."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.66,0:24:39.06,EN,,0,0,0,,"The sea of advertising, there is an aggressive propagandistic nature of
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.08,0:24:43.10,EN,,0,0,0,,the advertising itself. Deanonymization of age for the sake of advertising."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.13,0:24:45.57,EN,,0,0,0,,"As a result, this is no longer a wiki farm,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.59,0:24:47.43,EN,,0,0,0,,this is an advertising platform."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.45,0:24:50.45,EN,,0,0,0,,—"There was a sense of security and stability under Gamepedia
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.48,0:24:53.24,EN,,0,0,0,,that I don't think has carried over with the migration to Fandom."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.26,0:24:56.79,EN,,0,0,0,,—"Fandom's actions demonstrate that it cares about profits over quality
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.82,0:25:00.83,EN,,0,0,0,,and editor freedom, to the detriment of this wiki. It's time to go."
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.85,0:25:04.23,EN,,0,0,0,,—"Overall, as long as we fork to somewhere other than Fandom,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.26,0:25:05.82,EN,,0,0,0,,I'm going to be happy with the result."
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.85,0:25:07.65,EN,,0,0,0,,So while the best option wasn't clear,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.67,0:25:09.79,EN,,0,0,0,,the worst option definitely was.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.81,0:25:12.10,EN,,0,0,0,,So if nothing else, the fork was gonna happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.12,0:25:13.99,EN,,0,0,0,,But where the fork do we fork to?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.02,0:25:15.37,EN,,0,0,0,,That's a forkin' good question.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.39,0:25:18.43,EN,,0,0,0,,They could essentially choose any wiki farm that they wanted,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.46,0:25:20.18,EN,,0,0,0,,but there were four main options.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.20,0:25:23.26,EN,,0,0,0,,wiki.gg is a very popular Fandom alternative.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.29,0:25:25.61,EN,,0,0,0,,They host almost a thousand wikis currently,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.63,0:25:27.05,EN,,0,0,0,,including ones for games like
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.08,0:25:29.25,EN,,0,0,0,,Terraria, Risk of Rain, Ultrakill,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.28,0:25:30.12,EN,,0,0,0,,and of course,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.14,0:25:31.56,EN,,0,0,0,,Hello Kitty Island Adventure.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.59,0:25:35.14,EN,,0,0,0,,A lot of people like them because they're run by former Gamepedia employees,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.17,0:25:37.54,EN,,0,0,0,,including our old friend Donovan Duncan!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.57,0:25:39.46,EN,,0,0,0,,But that just shows that this option,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.49,0:25:40.40,EN,,0,0,0,,at the end of the day,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.43,0:25:42.28,EN,,0,0,0,,is just another corporate wiki farm.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.30,0:25:45.78,EN,,0,0,0,,And it'd be… kinda weird to say yes to Donovan once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.80,0:25:49.19,EN,,0,0,0,,Maybe going over there would make this whole thing happen all over again.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.21,0:25:53.58,EN,,0,0,0,,For something less corporate, they also considered ABXY, who host StrategyWiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.61,0:25:55.65,EN,,0,0,0,,This is their website, and, uh…
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.68,0:25:57.91,EN,,0,0,0,,This isn't even Web 1.0,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.93,0:25:59.01,EN,,0,0,0,,this is like, CERN.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.04,0:26:00.66,EN,,0,0,0,,They barely have any branding at all,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.69,0:26:03.90,EN,,0,0,0,,just this little Powered By StrategyWiki thing at the bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.92,0:26:05.65,EN,,0,0,0,,It's almost too little corporate oversight
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.68,0:26:08.35,EN,,0,0,0,,as they don't even have a global content delivery network.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.37,0:26:10.38,EN,,0,0,0,,all of the pages are hosted in America,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.41,0:26:13.27,EN,,0,0,0,,making the websites way slower for the rest of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.29,0:26:16.43,EN,,0,0,0,,especially with the huge traffic that the Minecraft wiki has.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.46,0:26:20.42,EN,,0,0,0,,There's also Bulbagarden, which hosts the Pokémon wiki on Bulbapedia.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.45,0:26:24.02,EN,,0,0,0,,They've allegedly denied buyout offers from Fandom multiple times over,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.05,0:26:26.24,EN,,0,0,0,,though I couldn't find any concrete evidence of this,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.27,0:26:28.29,EN,,0,0,0,,and they have a lot of experience in the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.31,0:26:31.09,EN,,0,0,0,,However, they don't allow for anonymous editing,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.12,0:26:33.20,EN,,0,0,0,,which is a dealbreaker for many people.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.23,0:26:35.34,EN,,0,0,0,,And one company actually reached out to them:
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.37,0:26:36.21,EN,,0,0,0,,Weird Gloop.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.24,0:26:39.48,EN,,0,0,0,,Their name and logo are based on a RuneScape item of the same name
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.50,0:26:40.96,EN,,0,0,0,,Remember how the RuneScape wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.98,0:26:42.96,EN,,0,0,0,,left Fandom because of the video ads?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.99,0:26:43.91,EN,,0,0,0,,This is them.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.93,0:26:45.74,EN,,0,0,0,,While there were some bad things about them,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.77,0:26:48.18,EN,,0,0,0,,like their weirdness with which widgets one could wield,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.20,0:26:49.88,EN,,0,0,0,,they also had a lot of advantages.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.90,0:26:50.96,EN,,0,0,0,,It's a small company,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.99,0:26:53.16,EN,,0,0,0,,their website is fast and reliable,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.18,0:26:55.07,EN,,0,0,0,,they have full-time system admins,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.10,0:26:57.71,EN,,0,0,0,,and are very transparent about their business practices.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.74,0:26:59.34,EN,,0,0,0,,they also put their money where their mouth is,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.37,0:27:01.33,EN,,0,0,0,,and bought the domain that they would get
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.35,0:27:02.96,EN,,0,0,0,,if they switched over to Weird Gloop.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.98,0:27:04.78,EN,,0,0,0,,They were very much like Curse in that way,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.80,0:27:07.96,EN,,0,0,0,,doing everything that they could to make sure that they were the main pick.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.98,0:27:09.53,EN,,0,0,0,,And while researching for this video,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.55,0:27:13.26,EN,,0,0,0,,they seemed to just be very professional in the way that they operate their business.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.28,0:27:15.23,EN,,0,0,0,,Like, it really looks like they know what they're doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.25,0:27:19.55,EN,,0,0,0,,All these options have their own ups and downs with Weird Gloop slightly in the lead,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.58,0:27:21.74,EN,,0,0,0,,but there's an unavoidable problem with all of them,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.77,0:27:23.88,EN,,0,0,0,,which goes back to where we started this whole thing:
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.90,0:27:25.07,EN,,0,0,0,,Search results.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.09,0:27:28.24,EN,,0,0,0,,Basically, from what I can understand, there's this thing called SEO,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.27,0:27:30.04,EN,,0,0,0,,search engine optimization.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.06,0:27:32.03,EN,,0,0,0,,It's basically a bunch of things that you can do
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.05,0:27:35.24,EN,,0,0,0,,to try to get your website to show up higher in the search results.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.26,0:27:37.22,EN,,0,0,0,,Being on the first page is very powerful,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.24,0:27:39.35,EN,,0,0,0,,and being the first link is the goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.38,0:27:41.34,EN,,0,0,0,,How do you increase your SEO?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.05,0:27:46.39,EN,,0,0,0,,That's the funny thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.41,0:27:48.41,EN,,0,0,0,,nobody fucking knows!!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.44,0:27:50.98,EN,,0,0,0,,Okay, well, Google has an article about SEO
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.00,0:27:52.36,EN,,0,0,0,,with some general tips
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.39,0:27:55.03,EN,,0,0,0,,but as far as some magical way to be at the top,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.06,0:27:56.53,EN,,0,0,0,,that doesn't exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.55,0:27:58.53,EN,,0,0,0,,Because if it did, everyone would do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.55,0:28:02.21,EN,,0,0,0,,Companies pay big money to people called SEO specialists
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.24,0:28:06.09,EN,,0,0,0,,whose sole purpose in life is to optimize websites for search engines.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.11,0:28:09.55,EN,,0,0,0,,It generally seems to prioritize bigger, interconnected websites,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.57,0:28:13.00,EN,,0,0,0,,with more content and more links that more visitors spend more time on.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.03,0:28:17.52,EN,,0,0,0,,And it just so happens that Fandom is in the top 50 most visited websites
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.54,0:28:18.71,EN,,0,0,0,,in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.74,0:28:19.85,EN,,0,0,0,,I don't think you understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.88,0:28:21.45,EN,,0,0,0,,Fandom is more popular
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.48,0:28:22.94,EN,,0,0,0,,than the fucking weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.97,0:28:23.85,EN,,0,0,0,,As we saw earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.87,0:28:27.01,EN,,0,0,0,,that means that it very often gets put at the top of search results,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.03,0:28:29.22,EN,,0,0,0,,despite being worse than the other options.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.25,0:28:31.24,EN,,0,0,0,,This was the biggest fear before the merge,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.26,0:28:35.12,EN,,0,0,0,,that even if they went through all the work of moving the wiki to another website,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.15,0:28:38.56,EN,,0,0,0,,the Fandom results would snuff them out and it would all be for nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.59,0:28:42.79,EN,,0,0,0,,However, one of these companies has actually been able to beat Fandom in the search results.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.82,0:28:44.13,EN,,0,0,0,,And that's Weird Gloop.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.16,0:28:48.22,EN,,0,0,0,,The RuneScape wikis have had some success with overtaking Fandom in the results
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.24,0:28:49.88,EN,,0,0,0,,and that was super valuable.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.91,0:28:51.21,EN,,0,0,0,,With all of its advantages,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.23,0:28:52.88,EN,,0,0,0,,Once Weird Gloop was on the table,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.91,0:28:56.07,EN,,0,0,0,,it was very quickly the favorite of the people on the wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.09,0:28:57.10,EN,,0,0,0,,A big vote was held,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.13,0:29:01.38,EN,,0,0,0,,and it was decided that Weird Gloop would be the host of the new Minecraft wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.41,0:29:04.45,EN,,0,0,0,,To make sure that it would be easier if they ever had to do this again,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.48,0:29:08.15,EN,,0,0,0,,the people at the Minecraft wiki have a list of agreements with Weird Gloop.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.17,0:29:11.07,EN,,0,0,0,,This is written for everyone to see on the Minecraft meta wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.09,0:29:12.34,EN,,0,0,0,,(link in the description, of course).
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.37,0:29:15.04,EN,,0,0,0,,Basically, if either party wants out, they can leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.06,0:29:17.44,EN,,0,0,0,,Weird Gloop will give the minecraft.wiki domain
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.47,0:29:19.27,EN,,0,0,0,,to someone trustworthy in the community,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.29,0:29:21.40,EN,,0,0,0,,give them all of the data contained in the wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.43,0:29:23.59,EN,,0,0,0,,and they can do basically whatever they want with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.62,0:29:27.53,EN,,0,0,0,,Now, all there is left to do is move everything once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.17,0:29:32.17,EN,,0,0,0,,On September 24th, 2023,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.19,0:29:35.53,EN,,0,0,0,,the wiki was officially forked to minecraft.wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.55,0:29:37.52,EN,,0,0,0,,While the Fandom wiki does still exist,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.55,0:29:41.62,EN,,0,0,0,,almost all of the people who worked on the Fandom wiki moved over to the new one.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.64,0:29:42.91,EN,,0,0,0,,In practice, this means that it
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.94,0:29:45.97,EN,,0,0,0,,basically looks incomplete compared to the Minecraft wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.99,0:29:47.71,EN,,0,0,0,,especially when it comes to new features.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.73,0:29:50.56,EN,,0,0,0,,It's been a little more than a year now since the wiki forked,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:50.59,0:29:53.48,EN,,0,0,0,,and they've actually been doing way better than they were on Fandom.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.51,0:29:56.94,EN,,0,0,0,,They recently put out an article about their first year being independent,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.96,0:29:58.67,EN,,0,0,0,,And that shows that—believe it or not—
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.69,0:30:03.20,EN,,0,0,0,,being on a website that doesn't bombard you with gigantic ads every single millisecond
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.23,0:30:04.77,EN,,0,0,0,,makes people want to visit you more.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.79,0:30:06.22,EN,,0,0,0,,It's kind of crazy, I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.24,0:30:07.95,EN,,0,0,0,,And while, as we saw earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.98,0:30:10.57,EN,,0,0,0,,a lot of those search results still have Fandom on top,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.60,0:30:13.37,EN,,0,0,0,,For most of the new features, the new wiki wins.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.39,0:30:15.96,EN,,0,0,0,,Much like what happened earlier with Redstone Wire Ltd,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:15.99,0:30:18.28,EN,,0,0,0,,There is now a company that manages the wiki:
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.31,0:30:19.66,EN,,0,0,0,,Block & Quill Ltd.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.69,0:30:21.13,EN,,0,0,0,,They have two permanent positions,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.15,0:30:23.65,EN,,0,0,0,,as well as five elected board member positions
Dialogue: 0,0:30:23.67,0:30:25.70,EN,,0,0,0,,that go up for election every single year
Dialogue: 0,0:30:25.73,0:30:27.70,EN,,0,0,0,,using Schulze method ranked choice voting
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.72,0:30:29.19,EN,,0,0,0,,because they're fucking nerds.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.21,0:30:30.38,EN,,0,0,0,,I don't really know how that works,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.40,0:30:33.60,EN,,0,0,0,,But I assume CGP Grey will make a video on it any year now.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.62,0:30:35.88,EN,,0,0,0,,Some people are still over on the Fandom wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.90,0:30:39.61,EN,,0,0,0,,just keeping vandalism at bay and adding stuff very slowly,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.64,0:30:40.74,EN,,0,0,0,,and that's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.76,0:30:41.60,EN,,0,0,0,,And I should mention—
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.62,0:30:44.66,EN,,0,0,0,,Please don't vandalize any of the wikis I've mentioned in this video.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.69,0:30:47.94,EN,,0,0,0,,An actual human being is gonna have to go and fix that.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.96,0:30:50.91,EN,,0,0,0,,Vandalizing the actual wikis doesn't hurt Fandom at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.94,0:30:52.39,EN,,0,0,0,,So… please don't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.42,0:30:54.30,EN,,0,0,0,,If you do want to hurt Fandom, though,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.32,0:30:57.09,EN,,0,0,0,,the best way to do that is to stop using their website.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.11,0:30:59.80,EN,,0,0,0,,you can do that by just not choosing it in the search results,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.83,0:31:02.81,EN,,0,0,0,,or there's a Chrome extension called Indie Wiki Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.84,0:31:06.53,EN,,0,0,0,,It redirects from all Fandom wikis to their independent alternatives.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.56,0:31:08.70,EN,,0,0,0,,Not sponsored, it's just a good extension.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.72,0:31:12.21,EN,,0,0,0,,Doesn't matter if it's Minecraft or RuneScape or any of these games,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.24,0:31:14.01,EN,,0,0,0,,it'll redirect you to the right place,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.04,0:31:17.04,EN,,0,0,0,,so looking up "redstone minecraft" will look like this instead,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.06,0:31:20.97,EN,,0,0,0,,with the link grayed out, and a link to the same article on the independent wiki.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.99,0:31:23.49,EN,,0,0,0,,It'll actually rearrange the search results for you,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.52,0:31:26.50,EN,,0,0,0,,which was kind of annoying when making this exact video,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.53,0:31:28.96,EN,,0,0,0,,but it'll probably be useful to you in normal gameplay.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.98,0:31:31.64,EN,,0,0,0,,There's also a mod that has been made for the actual game
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.67,0:31:35.33,EN,,0,0,0,,that opens a tab on the wiki for the block or item that you're looking at
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.35,0:31:36.53,EN,,0,0,0,,when you press H.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.55,0:31:38.76,EN,,0,0,0,,Not quite my tempo, but I figured I should mention it.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.78,0:31:39.90,EN,,0,0,0,,And also, I want to mention that,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.92,0:31:42.41,EN,,0,0,0,,if you're interested in more of the history of the wiki,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.43,0:31:44.74,EN,,0,0,0,,including a bunch of stuff that I couldn't include here,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.77,0:31:46.99,EN,,0,0,0,,you should go check out this page on the wiki about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.01,0:31:49.16,EN,,0,0,0,,It was super useful while researching this video
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.18,0:31:52.19,EN,,0,0,0,,to get the general vibe of the situation at any given time,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.21,0:31:54.22,EN,,0,0,0,,and the guy who made the page, TreeIsLife,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:54.25,0:31:56.43,EN,,0,0,0,,was super helpful and looked over the script for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.45,0:31:58.22,EN,,0,0,0,,While we're talking about people going over the script
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.25,0:32:01.49,EN,,0,0,0,,I also wanna thank Harristic for going over the part about the fork.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.51,0:32:04.21,EN,,0,0,0,,They both offered a lot of personal experience with this wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.24,0:32:07.16,EN,,0,0,0,,and I really appreciate them for giving their time to help me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.80,0:32:33.63,EN,,0,0,0,,Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.65,0:32:36.27,EN,,0,0,0,,I wanted to get this video out before Christmas…
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.81,0:32:38.49,EN,,0,0,0,,But, uh, that didn't happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.51,0:32:40.73,EN,,0,0,0,,Cause I'm recording it on Christmas day right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.98,0:32:45.41,EN,,0,0,0,,So let's just pretend that this set was decorated for Kwanzaa.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.43,0:32:46.28,EN,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.30,0:32:51.46,EN,,0,0,0,,I really appreciate everything I've been able to do this year on this channel.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.27,0:32:53.52,EN,,0,0,0,,It has been great…
Dialogue: 0,0:32:54.24,0:32:57.12,EN,,0,0,0,,…seeing that people actually like something that I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.15,0:32:59.17,EN,,0,0,0,,I wasn't trained in video editing,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.20,0:33:02.67,EN,,0,0,0,,I wasn't ever trained in writing or anything…
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.69,0:33:04.92,EN,,0,0,0,,I just kind of learned it myself, and…
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.94,0:33:06.70,EN,,0,0,0,,People like it. It means the world to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.73,0:33:07.69,EN,,0,0,0,,Seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.71,0:33:08.73,EN,,0,0,0,,Like, I—
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.25,0:33:10.46,EN,,0,0,0,,It— it's insane.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.38,0:33:13.28,EN,,0,0,0,,It's insane.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.31,0:33:14.18,EN,,0,0,0,,And yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:14.92,0:33:17.18,EN,,0,0,0,,I don't know what to say, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.21,0:33:19.73,EN,,0,0,0,,I just said I would turn on the camera
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.76,0:33:21.12,EN,,0,0,0,,and just start talking, but…
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.84,0:33:25.80,EN,,0,0,0,,I don't… really know what to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.82,0:33:27.53,EN,,0,0,0,,This is gonna be hell to edit, sorry Dime.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.06,0:33:28.92,EN,,0,0,0,,Anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.13,0:33:31.67,EN,,0,0,0,,Thank you. Seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.70,0:33:33.55,EN,,0,0,0,,Merry Christmas. Happy new year.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.89,0:33:35.90,EN,,0,0,0,,Merry, uh, Kwanzaa.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.93,0:33:38.35,EN,,0,0,0,,This set is decorated for Kwanzaa, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.69,0:33:39.53,EN,,0,0,0,,Definitely.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.55,0:33:42.41,EN,,0,0,0,,Just… be on the lookout for more stuff from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.44,0:33:45.74,EN,,0,0,0,,I love making videos, I want to keep making videos,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.76,0:33:47.72,EN,,0,0,0,,I'm excited for the future of this channel.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.75,0:33:52.04,EN,,0,0,0,,Happy winter solstice celebration, whatever one you have in your culture.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.07,0:33:55.32,EN,,0,0,0,,Now if you'll excuse me, I have to open the presents.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.24,0:34:01.69,EN,,0,0,0,,Ey. That's nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.61,0:00:07.61,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(961.56,177.89)}翻译/压制/字幕制作：HAF半个水果\N♡无偿翻译，用爱发电♡
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.79,0:00:13.79,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(967.56,109.89)}使用AI工具翻译，如有不准确的地方请在弹幕或评论区指正，谢谢！
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.19,0:00:24.19,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(981.56,127.89)}翻译质量权威评价：原来25年就有小拉即用机翻糊弄人了
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.56,0:00:04.83,CN,,0,0,0,,—你心目中的我的世界维基是什么样子的？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.85,0:00:06.89,CN,,0,0,0,,你想到了什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.92,0:00:08.30,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你想到了苹果
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.32,0:00:09.82,CN,,0,0,0,,那你就有问题了
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.84,0:00:12.21,CN,,0,0,0,,一个游戏对维基的依赖......
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.23,0:00:14.18,CN,,0,0,0,,信不信由你，我并不是它的最大粉丝
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.21,0:00:15.95,CN,,0,0,0,,但事情到了这个地步，差不多就是这样了
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.97,0:00:17.48,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你想学红石
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.50,0:00:19.30,CN,,0,0,0,,要么你击败一座古城
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.32,0:00:20.36,CN,,0,0,0,,要么找到一座丛林神庙
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.39,0:00:22.60,CN,,0,0,0,,或者在Google上搜索“我的世界 红石”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.63,0:00:23.99,CN,,0,0,0,,那么你选哪一个呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.01,0:00:25.63,CN,,0,0,0,,我想我会称这个问题为“维基问题”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.65,0:00:27.16,CN,,0,0,0,,不过那是另一个时间的故事了
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.19,0:00:29.92,CN,,0,0,0,,我们今天感兴趣的是那次搜索的结果
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.94,0:00:32.09,CN,,0,0,0,,最靠前的是一个名为“Fandom”的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.12,0:00:33.44,CN,,0,0,0,,而它们两个……都很糟糕
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:35.58,CN,,0,0,0,,进入之后就问我年龄
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.60,0:00:38.72,CN,,0,0,0,,我不确定为什么我的世界维基如此关心这种事情
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.75,0:00:39.60,CN,,0,0,0,,然而
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.62,0:00:43.23,CN,,0,0,0,,用途部分读起来就像有人凭记忆列出了红石能做的所有事情
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.25,0:00:45.52,CN,,0,0,0,,然后就这样了
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.55,0:00:49.65,CN,,0,0,0,,旁边有一堆随机页面的建议，比如“凋灵风暴”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.68,0:00:52.54,CN,,0,0,0,,我很确定那只是在故事模式里
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.56,0:00:55.58,CN,,0,0,0,,我打赌你现在已经注意到，看起来我们像是要得到1500万积分
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.61,0:00:57.50,CN,,0,0,0,,因为顶部有一个视频广告
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.52,0:00:58.83,CN,,0,0,0,,边栏有横幅广告
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.85,0:01:00.25,CN,,0,0,0,,角落里还有视频广告
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.27,0:01:03.27,CN,,0,0,0,,而我真正需要的信息只有一小部分
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.30,0:01:04.53,CN,,0,0,0,,如果我们进入第二条搜索结果—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.56,0:01:05.95,CN,,0,0,0,,开什么玩笑，相信我 bro—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.98,0:01:06.95,CN,,0,0,0,,与第一条的页面一样
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.98,0:01:09.35,CN,,0,0,0,,广告甚至比上一个还要多
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.37,0:01:10.92,CN,,0,0,0,,这个提供的信息多一些
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.95,0:01:13.64,CN,,0,0,0,,但仍然没有在配方列表中加入合成器
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.11,0:01:13.68,CN,,0,0,0,,{\pos(1390,460)}*做完这个视频后就加入了
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.67,0:01:16.25,CN,,0,0,0,,涂蜡的氧化铜灯就只是个问号？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.28,0:01:19.12,CN,,0,0,0,,你知道，也许这就是一个由粉丝维护的维基之类的
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.15,0:01:21.39,CN,,0,0,0,,毕竟它是在一个叫Fandom的网站上
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.41,0:01:24.65,CN,,0,0,0,,让我们点击2009年这个随机的维基链接
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.68,0:01:25.94,CN,,0,0,0,,这应该带我们进入真—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.40,0:01:27.23,CN,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.26,0:01:28.61,CN,,0,0,0,,又回到Fandom了
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.63,0:01:29.68,CN,,0,0,0,,这是真的
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.70,0:01:32.18,CN,,0,0,0,,太可惜了，这太糟糕了
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.20,0:01:35.28,CN,,0,0,0,,我记得以前维基看起来很专业
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.30,0:01:37.16,CN,,0,0,0,,维基怎么就变成
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.18,0:01:38.02,CN,,0,0,0,,这样了？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.04,0:01:40.59,CN,,0,0,0,,它怎么会落到 Fandom 这样的公司手里
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.61,0:01:42.87,CN,,0,0,0,,一个人人喊打的公司
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.90,0:01:44.55,CN,,0,0,0,,因为他们总是想
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.58,0:01:47.74,CN,,0,0,0,,从用户身上尽可能多地吸金？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.77,0:01:50.55,CN,,0,0,0,,维基最近到底是怎么变得越来越好的？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.58,0:01:54.55,CN,,0,0,0,,要想知道答案，让我们访问 2009 年的维基网站
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.48,0:02:16.58,CN,,0,0,0,,故事开始于 Mojang 论坛
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.61,0:02:18.57,CN,,0,0,0,,他们那时刚刚制作了一款积木小游戏
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.60,0:02:20.14,CN,,0,0,0,,开始有点流行
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.17,0:02:23.81,CN,,0,0,0,,而论坛并不具备应对如此大规模人群的能力
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.83,0:02:26.81,CN,,0,0,0,,所以一个名叫 CitricSquid 的用户在他17岁时
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.84,0:02:28.89,CN,,0,0,0,,搭建了一个非官方的我的世界论坛
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.92,0:02:31.12,CN,,0,0,0,,制作积木游戏的人说，这是
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.14,0:02:33.35,CN,,0,0,0,,比官方论坛还“要要好”
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.37,0:02:35.75,CN,,0,0,0,,甚至将 mojang.com 上的论坛给关了
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.77,0:02:37.99,CN,,0,0,0,,用户 Quatroking 建议 CitricSquid
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.01,0:02:41.68,CN,,0,0,0,,我的世界维基与论坛结合起来将非常有用
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.71,0:02:44.80,CN,,0,0,0,,Citric 同意了。所以在 2009 年 6 月 17 日
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.82,0:02:46.84,CN,,0,0,0,,他注册了 minecraftwiki.net 这个域名
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.86,0:02:48.20,CN,,0,0,0,,使用了 MediaWiki 这个开源维基系统
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.23,0:02:51.11,CN,,0,0,0,,这个维基软件基本上地球人都在用
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.13,0:02:53.07,CN,,0,0,0,,并让 Quatro 负责审核它
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.09,0:02:56.05,CN,,0,0,0,,Mojang 最终会将这些页面链接到 minecraft.net 上
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.08,0:02:58.93,CN,,0,0,0,,使它们几乎成为社区的官方网站
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.96,0:03:02.01,CN,,0,0,0,,一开始，维基实际上并没有什么用
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.04,0:03:03.83,CN,,0,0,0,,因为游戏还很简陋
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.86,0:03:06.96,CN,,0,0,0,,在当时，你只能从一块石头上了解到这么多
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.99,0:03:08.98,CN,,0,0,0,,直到增加了合成系统
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.01,0:03:11.39,CN,,0,0,0,,游戏中无法查看合成表
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.42,0:03:13.90,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上需要维基才能玩生存模式
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.93,0:03:16.00,CN,,0,0,0,,这意味着，维基的受欢迎程度现在
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.03,0:03:18.30,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上与游戏的成功与否挂钩
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.32,0:03:21.26,CN,,0,0,0,,And, uh, 我的世界算是……相当成功
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.29,0:03:22.79,CN,,0,0,0,,越来越多的人来浏览网站
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.81,0:03:25.33,CN,,0,0,0,,CitricSquid 在服务器上的开销也越来越大
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.35,0:03:29.13,CN,,0,0,0,,访问的人太多了，他花光了积蓄来续费这些服务器
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.16,0:03:31.22,CN,,0,0,0,,他从 aera(昵称) 获得了一些资助
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.24,0:03:34.00,CN,,0,0,0,,顺便说一下，他是第一个拥有多个世界的我的世界服务器的人
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.02,0:03:36.74,CN,,0,0,0,,但维基的增长速度仍然非常快
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.76,0:03:40.57,CN,,0,0,0,,2010 年，网站的平均访问量
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.60,0:03:43.15,CN,,0,0,0,,曾连续两个月每周翻一番
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.17,0:03:46.92,CN,,0,0,0,,Citric 后来说，维持这两个网站的运行
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.95,0:03:48.60,CN,,0,0,0,,每月要花费数万美元
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.63,0:03:53.01,CN,,0,0,0,,他们曾经举行过一次大型捐款活动，募集到大约 3500 美元
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.04,0:03:54.74,CN,,0,0,0,,因为情况开始变得有点不妙
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.76,0:03:57.31,CN,,0,0,0,,他们实在不想再向别人讨钱了
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.33,0:03:59.98,CN,,0,0,0,,他不得不加了一个广告，这让人有点难过
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.01,0:04:01.19,CN,,0,0,0,,但他们也只能这样了
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.22,0:04:04.67,CN,,0,0,0,,由广告产生的收入，他们还注册了一家
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.69,0:04:07.43,CN,,0,0,0,,名为 Redstone Wire Ltd 的公司来管理这些收入
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.45,0:04:09.87,CN,,0,0,0,,此时，压力真的很大
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.90,0:04:12.70,CN,,0,0,0,,“我们仍然面临着快速增长的流量和成本，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.72,0:04:14.28,CN,,0,0,0,,这些都是我们无法跟上的。”
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.30,0:04:16.62,CN,,0,0,0,,“WedTM、aera和我（都是志愿者）
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.65,0:04:19.82,CN,,0,0,0,,是唯一参与日常运营的人，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.85,0:04:21.95,CN,,0,0,0,,WedTM有自己的全职工作，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.97,0:04:25.79,CN,,0,0,0,,aera有自己的生意要经营，而我在技术上一窍不通，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.82,0:04:29.34,CN,,0,0,0,,3个志愿者运营的网站现在比Stackoverflow还大。”
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.37,0:04:33.66,CN,,0,0,0,,—你能想象托管这款游戏如此重要的东西的压力吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.69,0:04:35.46,CN,,0,0,0,,谁知道他们能坚持多久！
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.49,0:04:37.15,CN,,0,0,0,,如果游戏变得更受欢迎，那么
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.18,0:04:38.77,CN,,0,0,0,,他们到底要怎么办——
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.79,0:04:39.70,CN,,0,0,0,,Uh—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.96,0:04:47.80,CN,,0,0,0,,喂？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.65,0:04:52.46,CN,,0,0,0,,你想买下维基和论坛吗？？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.48,0:04:54.49,CN,,0,0,0,,Redstone Wire 成立两个月后
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.52,0:04:58.89,CN,,0,0,0,,他们被 Curse LLC 的内容总监 Donovan Duncan 联系了
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.91,0:05:01.25,CN,,0,0,0,,当时，Curse 的主要竞争对手是 Wikia
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.28,0:05:04.39,CN,,0,0,0,,正在做出一些非常......反消费者的决定
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.42,0:05:06.78,CN,,0,0,0,,他们强迫其网站上的每个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.81,0:05:08.79,CN,,0,0,0,,都从这个皮肤切换为......
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.82,0:05:10.12,CN,,0,0,0,,这样
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.20,0:05:13.27,CN,,0,0,0,,它的宽度被锁定，自定义功能较少
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.29,0:05:14.89,CN,,0,0,0,,一堆你不关心的内容
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.91,0:05:17.79,CN,,0,0,0,,总之，感觉 Wikia 试图把你
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.82,0:05:19.60,CN,,0,0,0,,从正在看的维基中拉出来
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.63,0:05:22.22,CN,,0,0,0,,没人要求这个。什么都没破坏
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.25,0:05:23.86,CN,,0,0,0,,但他们还是修复了它
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.88,0:05:25.64,CN,,0,0,0,,而它
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.67,0:05:26.73,CN,,0,0,0,,我的意思是页面的宽度
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.75,0:05:28.60,CN,,0,0,0,,Oasis 主题公布后不久
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.62,0:05:31.18,CN,,0,0,0,,庞大的魔兽世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.21,0:05:34.72,CN,,0,0,0,,正在考虑离开，他们决定转到Curse
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.75,0:05:37.37,CN,,0,0,0,,随着这次胜利，Curse准备进行一些赚钱的举措
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.40,0:05:41.14,CN,,0,0,0,,其中之一就是确保庞大的我的世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.16,0:05:43.90,CN,,0,0,0,,在财务困境期间不会转到Wikia
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.93,0:05:47.46,CN,,0,0,0,,Donovan 提出从 Redstone Wire 购买维基和论坛
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.48,0:05:50.59,CN,,0,0,0,,并聘请公司的三名成员到 Curse 工作
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.62,0:05:52.88,CN,,0,0,0,,大公司将负责运营后端
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.90,0:05:55.80,CN,,0,0,0,,而 Redstone Wire 的员工可以专注于社区
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.82,0:05:59.32,CN,,0,0,0,,因此，Citric 的选择是，要么继续走这条独立的道路
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.34,0:06:00.73,CN,,0,0,0,,没有明确的前进方向
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.75,0:06:03.09,CN,,0,0,0,,不知道下个月维基是否还会存在
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.11,0:06:05.90,CN,,0,0,0,,不知道在接下来的几年里游戏是否会有更大的发展
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.93,0:06:07.32,CN,,0,0,0,,剧透一下，它会
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.35,0:06:11.17,CN,,0,0,0,,总之，要让这个 18 岁的孩子肩负起巨大的压力
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.19,0:06:12.03,CN,,0,0,0,,或者…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.37,0:06:13.98,CN,,0,0,0,,他们可以直接答应 Donovan
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.00,0:06:15.36,CN,,0,0,0,,你会怎么选呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.38,0:06:17.15,CN,,0,0,0,,我想我应该把这个问题叫做 “Donovan问题”
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.92,0:06:20.88,CN,,0,0,0,,无需多言，交易成功了
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.91,0:06:23.60,CN,,0,0,0,,Curse LLC 现在是维基的所有者
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.62,0:06:27.11,CN,,0,0,0,,不到一年后，Redstone Wire Ltd 永久解散
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.13,0:06:29.52,CN,,0,0,0,,这也说得通，因为之后他们拥有的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.54,0:06:33.01,CN,,0,0,0,,只有 minecraftmuseum.net 和 minecraftservers.com
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.04,0:06:34.92,CN,,0,0,0,,而这两个网站我连听都没听说过
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.95,0:06:35.84,CN,,0,0,0,,之后两年
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.87,0:06:38.87,CN,,0,0,0,,Curse 基本上会像往常一样拥有和运营我的世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.89,0:06:42.31,CN,,0,0,0,,一些版主被换来换去，一些小东西被改变了
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.34,0:06:44.57,CN,,0,0,0,,但从外表上看，什么都没发生
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.60,0:06:46.21,CN,,0,0,0,,唯一能证明 Curse 参与的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.23,0:06:49.08,CN,,0,0,0,,是底部的 Curse 标准页脚
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.11,0:06:50.26,CN,,0,0,0,,Curse 做了一件事
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.29,0:06:51.83,CN,,0,0,0,,那就是与 Mojang 签订了协议
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.85,0:06:53.80,CN,,0,0,0,,使维基正式成为官方维基
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.82,0:06:55.29,CN,,0,0,0,,实际上，这意味着
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.32,0:06:58.45,CN,,0,0,0,,Mojang 现在可以在网站上将其列为官方维基
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.47,0:07:01.67,CN,,0,0,0,,一年后，他们还更改了我的世界维基的标题
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.69,0:07:04.75,CN,,0,0,0,,从 “关于我的世界信息的最终来源 ”
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.77,0:07:07.95,CN,,0,0,0,,到 “关于我的世界信息的官方资源”
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.97,0:07:11.73,CN,,0,0,0,,哇，改了一个半字。真了不起
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.75,0:07:14.28,CN,,0,0,0,,问题的关键在于，这是对维基的某种道德使用
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.31,0:07:18.02,CN,,0,0,0,,我真的很敬佩他们，因为他们没有做太大的改动，而是努力使其正式化
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.04,0:07:20.54,CN,,0,0,0,,在此期间，Curse 还收购了许多其他维基站点
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.57,0:07:22.39,CN,,0,0,0,,截至 2012 年 9 月
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.41,0:07:23.66,CN,,0,0,0,,他们托管了 26 个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.69,0:07:26.32,CN,,0,0,0,,像 2D我的世界，中世纪我的世界
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.35,0:07:29.62,CN,,0,0,0,,辐射我的世界以及不如我的世界流行的我的世界
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.64,0:07:31.83,CN,,0,0,0,,他们已经拥有了大量的大型维基站点
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.85,0:07:33.72,CN,,0,0,0,,他们希望维基站点发展得更好
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.75,0:07:37.09,CN,,0,0,0,,不过，他们的实践方式已经很难再继续下去了
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.12,0:07:40.41,CN,,0,0,0,,每个维基的收购似乎都是一项非常私人的任务
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.44,0:07:42.01,CN,,0,0,0,,他们不可能永远这样做
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.04,0:07:46.06,CN,,0,0,0,,如果他们想与 Wikia 这样的公司竞争，就必须有所改变
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.08,0:07:48.48,CN,,0,0,0,,因此，2012 年，Curse 推出了 Hydra
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.50,0:07:50.88,CN,,0,0,0,,这是一款 MediaWiki 软件的定制版本
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.90,0:07:54.31,CN,,0,0,0,,其设计目的是在只有一个基础的情况下托管多个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.33,0:07:55.74,CN,,0,0,0,,哦，我知道他们为什么这么叫了
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.77,0:07:58.47,CN,,0,0,0,,他们不必再单独更新每个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.49,0:08:02.29,CN,,0,0,0,,而只需更新一个运行九头蛇的服务器就可以了
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.32,0:08:04.70,CN,,0,0,0,,这使得每个维基都不那么个性化
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.73,0:08:07.52,CN,,0,0,0,,所以如果他们愿意，他们可以拥有更多的维基
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.55,0:08:09.82,CN,,0,0,0,,由于这一发现，他们将Hydra放入
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.84,0:08:12.48,CN,,0,0,0,,自己的维基托管服务 Gamepedia 中
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.50,0:08:16.10,CN,,0,0,0,,你可以去 gamepedia.com 建议创建一个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.12,0:08:19.48,CN,,0,0,0,,如果他们得到足够的建议和许多的员工
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.50,0:08:21.66,CN,,0,0,0,,而Curse的员工个人喜欢它
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.68,0:08:24.81,CN,,0,0,0,,并且你猜中了这个魔法罐里的果冻豆数量
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.83,0:08:25.81,CN,,0,0,0,,他们就会实现它
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.83,0:08:30.36,CN,,0,0,0,,它们都会托管在 gamepedia.com 上，并带有游戏名称的子域名
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.38,0:08:33.49,CN,,0,0,0,,所以在2013年9月，我的世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.52,0:08:37.61,CN,,0,0,0,,托管在更笨重的URL minecraft.gamepedia.com 上
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.63,0:08:39.55,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你不会英语
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.57,0:08:41.56,CN,,0,0,0,,情况就更糟了，因为链接中会包含语言
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.59,0:08:45.84,CN,,0,0,0,,所以，德语用户必须访问 minecraft-de.gamepedia.com
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.86,0:08:47.78,CN,,0,0,0,,供参考，以下是我的信用卡号
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.81,0:08:49.28,CN,,0,0,0,,尽管它在一个新网站上
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.30,0:08:50.93,CN,,0,0,0,,所有旧链接仍然有效
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.96,0:08:53.69,CN,,0,0,0,,但它们会重定向到 Gamepedia 上的相关页面
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.71,0:08:54.81,CN,,0,0,0,,好了，总结一下：
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.84,0:08:58.73,CN,,0,0,0,,Gamepedia 是所有 Gamepedia 维基的托管服务名称
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.76,0:09:01.83,CN,,0,0,0,,它使用 MediaWiki 的定制构建  Hydra
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.86,0:09:04.84,CN,,0,0,0,,所有维基都托管在 Gamepedia 网站上
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.86,0:09:08.46,CN,,0,0,0,,Gamepedia 是 Curse Media 的一个部门
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.49,0:09:12.10,CN,,0,0,0,,而 Curse Media 是 Curse LLC 公司的一个部门
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.13,0:09:13.19,CN,,0,0,0,,其实很简单！
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.21,0:09:15.75,CN,,0,0,0,,Curse Media 还设有 Curse Network 等部门
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.77,0:09:17.41,CN,,0,0,0,,负责管理许多游戏的论坛
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.43,0:09:19.01,CN,,0,0,0,,包括我的世界论坛
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.04,0:09:20.50,CN,,0,0,0,,此外还有 Curse Entertainment
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.53,0:09:21.74,CN,,0,0,0,,负责现场活动
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.77,0:09:24.50,CN,,0,0,0,,和其他一些疯狂的事情，我就不一一赘述了
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.52,0:09:26.53,CN,,0,0,0,,Hydra 于 2012 年 9 月问世
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.55,0:09:28.30,CN,,0,0,0,,八个月内托管的维基数量
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.33,0:09:31.03,CN,,0,0,0,,是之前的十倍
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.06,0:09:33.45,CN,,0,0,0,,这意味着 Gamepedia 不仅仅是一个维基托管商
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.47,0:09:36.10,CN,,0,0,0,,他们实际上还拥有一个布满维基的农场
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.12,0:09:40.01,CN,,0,0,0,,这就是为什么只要有一堆维基聚集在一个地方，就会被称为维基农场的原因
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.04,0:09:41.77,CN,,0,0,0,,当然，除非它是一个维基动物园
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.80,0:09:43.54,CN,,0,0,0,,这本身并不坏
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.57,0:09:47.97,CN,,0,0,0,,但现在我的世界维基突然变成了一个巨大维基农场的一小部分
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.99,0:09:51.15,CN,,0,0,0,,尽管它是 Gamepedia 上最受欢迎的维基
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.18,0:09:53.82,CN,,0,0,0,,但也只是数百个维基中的一个
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.85,0:09:56.37,CN,,0,0,0,,只有这么多的关心和关注可以分配
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.39,0:09:59.02,CN,,0,0,0,,我的世界维基正式转移到 Gamepedia
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.05,0:10:01.59,CN,,0,0,0,,日期为2013年9月19日星期四
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.61,0:10:04.15,CN,,0,0,0,,正好在我的世界的巅峰人气之后
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.18,0:10:07.08,CN,,0,0,0,,在大多数人的印象中，维基看起来......有点像这样
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.11,0:10:10.01,CN,,0,0,0,,要么属于 Curse，要么已经在 Gamepedia 上了
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.03,0:10:13.94,CN,,0,0,0,,Curse 是当时互联网上最专业的视频游戏公司之一
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.94,0:10:17.62,CN,,0,0,0,,他们有一个多频道网络，一个TeamSpeak的竞争对手，一个电子竞技团队……
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.65,0:10:20.24,CN,,0,0,0,,你知道那些旧的mcspotlight视频吗？他们制作的
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.26,0:10:23.22,CN,,0,0,0,,直到今天，他们仍然通过他们现在的公司霸主
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.24,0:10:25.84,CN,,0,0,0,,Overwolf运营CurseForge进行模组制作
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.86,0:10:30.10,CN,,0,0,0,,而 Curse 在很大程度上做得很漂亮......还不错，我猜，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.13,0:10:33.56,CN,,0,0,0,,还有一些关于 Bukkit 的东西，这是另一个故事了......
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.58,0:10:37.81,CN,,0,0,0,,他们有巨大的右侧边栏，只是为了显示来自 Mojang 的推文，出于某种原因...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.84,0:10:39.86,CN,,0,0,0,,顺便说一句，他们花了两年时间才把它移除
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.88,0:10:43.57,CN,,0,0,0,,不过，当时我们大多数人都还是孩子，我知道我从来没有注意到这些东西
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.59,0:10:45.97,CN,,0,0,0,,我只是用用维基，并没有多想
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.99,0:10:48.29,CN,,0,0,0,,他们基本上可以在互联网上做任何事情
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.31,0:10:50.28,CN,,0,0,0,,我觉得他们非常值得信赖
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.31,0:10:52.91,CN,,0,0,0,,看起来，他们只是一家典型的快速发展的科技公司
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.94,0:10:55.55,CN,,0,0,0,,通过大量烧钱，从而让人们爱上他们
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.58,0:10:59.19,CN,,0,0,0,,希望一家大公司将其从巨额债务中收购
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.21,0:11:01.91,CN,,0,0,0,,并教他们如何在燃烧所有商誉的同时赚钱
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.94,0:11:06.26,CN,,0,0,0,,创始人可以在 36 岁时退休并成为天使投资人
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.84,0:11:10.22,CN,,0,0,0,,事实也正是如此
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.24,0:11:15.01,CN,,0,0,0,,2016年，有一家叫 Twitch Interactive, Inc. 的小公司
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.04,0:11:16.11,CN,,0,0,0,,归亚马逊所有
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.13,0:11:19.50,CN,,0,0,0,,他们会买下 Curse LLC 及其所有子公司
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.53,0:11:24.29,CN,,0,0,0,,所以现在，Jeffrey pissbottle Bezos拥有我的世界维基和论坛
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.31,0:11:27.01,CN,,0,0,0,,大多数人并不真正记得我的世界社区中的这段时间
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.03,0:11:30.92,CN,,0,0,0,,因为 2016 年到 2018 年是我的世界的黑暗时代
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.95,0:11:33.62,CN,,0,0,0,,当时，众多的小怪被添加进来
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.64,0:11:36.03,CN,,0,0,0,,而我们却没有理由与它们互动
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.06,0:11:38.49,CN,,0,0,0,,这也是合成书被添加到游戏中的时候
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.51,0:11:43.03,CN,,0,0,0,,这使得维基在提供制作配方的重要作用现在完全无关紧要
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.06,0:11:46.25,CN,,0,0,0,,实际上，被亚马逊收购对维基来说并不是什么大事
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.27,0:11:47.88,CN,,0,0,0,,他们在那边并没有什么变化
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.90,0:11:49.69,CN,,0,0,0,,他们弄乱了论坛上的一些字体
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.71,0:11:53.44,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你把旧的论坛帖子用于视频或其他东西，那真的很烦人——
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.47,0:11:54.30,CN,,0,0,0,,谁干的？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.33,0:11:58.31,CN,,0,0,0,,他们让整个网站的所有登录系统都与 Twitch 同步，因为...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.34,0:11:59.18,CN,,0,0,0,,为什么不呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.20,0:12:01.32,CN,,0,0,0,,我想，CitricSquid 是在枪口的逼迫下
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.35,0:12:04.40,CN,,0,0,0,,才发布了这篇超级无聊的企业新闻稿
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.42,0:12:06.74,CN,,0,0,0,,“准备好你的 PogChamp 表情”？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.77,0:12:09.55,CN,,0,0,0,,“你会需要它的"？man ! 真对不起
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.58,0:12:11.92,CN,,0,0,0,,但总的来说，他们的表现并不差
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.95,0:12:15.42,CN,,0,0,0,,Twitch 当时的主要工作是为 Curse Client
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.45,0:12:16.63,CN,,0,0,0,,已更名为 Twitch App
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.65,0:12:21.27,CN,,0,0,0,,提供服务，如果你曾经使用过它，你就会知道它从一开始\N就是一个地狱般的可憎之物
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.29,0:12:24.63,CN,,0,0,0,,他们真的希望这个能成功，所以维基大部分被保留了下来
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.66,0:12:27.10,CN,,0,0,0,,Twitch 应用程序一直使用到 2022 年
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.13,0:12:29.26,CN,,0,0,0,,然后就被封杀了
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.28,0:12:31.90,CN,,0,0,0,,他们也从所有地方删除了所有关于它的内容
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.93,0:12:33.94,CN,,0,0,0,,但我不会忘记。我从未忘记
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.96,0:12:36.48,CN,,0,0,0,,不过，他们没有在维基上做手脚还真有点奇怪
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.50,0:12:39.62,CN,,0,0,0,,我不知道这次收购是否别有用心
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.16,0:12:42.24,CN,,0,0,0,,Knock knock.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.26,0:12:44.03,CN,,0,0,0,,这是 Fandom 公司
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.06,0:12:45.39,CN,,0,0,0,,有巨大的保险库
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.41,0:12:46.44,CN,,0,0,0,,有钱
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.47,0:12:47.65,CN,,0,0,0,,金库
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.68,0:12:49.30,CN,,0,0,0,,打开你的钱包
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.33,0:12:51.47,CN,,0,0,0,,不要再让他们倒闭了
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.50,0:12:55.65,CN,,0,0,0,,2018 年，Fandom 从 Twitch 收购了整个 Curse Media 部门
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.68,0:12:58.08,CN,,0,0,0,,这意味着 Curse 现在基本上一分为二
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.11,0:13:00.56,CN,,0,0,0,,维基和论坛转到 Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.58,0:13:03.31,CN,,0,0,0,,而 CurseForge 和 Twitch 应用程序将留在 Twitch
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.34,0:13:06.72,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你想知道Fandom在这整个过程中到底在做什么，嗯——
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.75,0:13:07.98,CN,,0,0,0,,surprise, surprise—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.00,0:13:11.07,CN,,0,0,0,,Fandom 只是我们的老朋友 Wikia 的新名字！
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.09,0:13:14.50,CN,,0,0,0,,没错，就是这家公司做出了如此反消费者的决定
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.53,0:13:17.30,CN,,0,0,0,,Curse 利用这种仇恨来推动自己的业务！
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.33,0:13:21.11,CN,,0,0,0,,他们的设计如此糟糕，以至于他们拥有的最大的维基网站
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.13,0:13:22.96,CN,,0,0,0,,在设计曝光几天后就离开了
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.99,0:13:27.12,CN,,0,0,0,,就在一年前，这些人还上线了自动播放的视频广告
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.14,0:13:30.42,CN,,0,0,0,,这些广告非常令人讨厌，以至于他们说服了 RuneScape wiki 跳槽
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.44,0:13:34.17,CN,,0,0,0,,并自己为维基付费，而不是 Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.20,0:13:38.79,CN,,0,0,0,,就是这些人买下了 Gamepedia 上的所有维基
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.73,0:13:40.71,CN,,0,0,0,,耶————
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.73,0:13:44.49,CN,,0,0,0,,我想从长远来看，Wikia 最终获得了我的世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.52,0:13:45.70,CN,,0,0,0,,等一下，等一下
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.72,0:13:47.73,CN,,0,0,0,,像 Fandom 这样的普通公司
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.76,0:13:50.58,CN,,0,0,0,,是如何从亚马逊购买整个部门的？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.61,0:13:53.41,CN,,0,0,0,,他们并不只是在 Prime Day 的时候才把它放到网站上
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.44,0:13:56.69,CN,,0,0,0,,也许 Bezos 那天只是觉得自己超级慷慨
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.71,0:14:01.37,CN,,0,0,0,,也可能是因为亚马逊在 2006 年向 Wikia 投资了一大笔钱
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.39,0:14:03.07,CN,,0,0,0,,具体多少钱我们不得而知
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.09,0:14:06.41,CN,,0,0,0,,但亚马逊表示，他们是 B 轮融资的唯一投资者
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.43,0:14:10.57,CN,,0,0,0,,{\pos(974,872)}而根据 Crunchbase，Wikia 在 B 轮融资中获得了 1000 万美元
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.71,0:14:10.39,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,0)\pos(978,974)}我认为这不可信，仅供参考
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.60,0:14:13.57,CN,,0,0,0,,所以我认为 “一大笔 ”是个不错的范围
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.60,0:14:16.69,CN,,0,0,0,,很高兴知道 Fandom 和亚马逊是好朋友
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.71,0:14:20.31,CN,,0,0,0,,真是......真是太棒了。他们是最好的朋友，知道吗？他们只是...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.33,0:14:22.19,CN,,0,0,0,,他们就在这里，面对这个世界
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.21,0:14:23.33,CN,,0,0,0,,他们同穿一条裤子
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.35,0:14:24.89,CN,,0,0,0,,他们是灵魂伴侣，他们彼此相爱
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.92,0:14:26.58,CN,,0,0,0,,他们在亲吻，他们在拥抱，他们在依偎
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.61,0:14:27.58,CN,,0,0,0,,我们喜欢看( *︾▽︾)
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.61,0:14:30.96,CN,,0,0,0,,非常巧合的是，就在这次收购前几个月
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.99,0:14:33.87,CN,,0,0,0,,Fandom被Integrated Media Company收购
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.90,0:14:38.36,CN,,0,0,0,,这是一家位于德克萨斯太平洋集团内的公司，一家私募股权公司
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.39,0:14:41.76,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你不知道私募股权基金是什么鬼东西，也不知道它为什么如此坚挺
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.79,0:14:44.14,CN,,0,0,0,,那么在制作这段视频之前，我也不知道
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.17,0:14:46.81,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上，它就像 “炒房客”，不过是百万富翁的 “炒房客”
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.84,0:14:51.09,CN,,0,0,0,,一群有钱的混蛋成立了 Ultron
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.12,0:14:54.20,CN,,0,0,0,,目的是贷款买下一家不知道如何赚钱的硅谷公司
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.23,0:14:57.12,CN,,0,0,0,,然后拼命提高公司价值
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.15,0:14:59.69,CN,,0,0,0,,以尽快偿还贷款
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.72,0:15:02.71,CN,,0,0,0,,最后，公司不欠银行一分钱
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.74,0:15:04.81,CN,,0,0,0,,现在他们拥有了一家大型科技公司
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.83,0:15:09.25,CN,,0,0,0,,收购 Fandom 的有钱混蛋掌舵人是 Jonathan Miller
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.27,0:15:13.29,CN,,0,0,0,,他曾在 Viacom 和 News Corporation 等有趣的公司工作过
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.31,0:15:15.45,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你想知道他的商业策略是什么
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.48,0:15:20.02,CN,,0,0,0,,2004 年，他在 AOL （美国在线）花费数亿美元
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.05,0:15:23.77,CN,,0,0,0,,收购了一家名为 advertising.com 的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.80,0:15:25.29,CN,,0,0,0,,advertising（广告）
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.32,0:15:26.70,CN,,0,0,0,,.com
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.72,0:15:30.01,CN,,0,0,0,,直接贴你脸上写了，天啊
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.03,0:15:32.57,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上，如果你认为亚马逊想要钱
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.59,0:15:37.36,CN,,0,0,0,,这些家伙更坏。他们现在控制着现存的所有 Gamepedia 维基
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.38,0:15:39.35,CN,,0,0,0,,TPG 已与许多...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.37,0:15:41.37,CN,,0,0,0,,过去伟大、令人惊叹的品牌合作过
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.39,0:15:43.93,CN,,0,0,0,,就像 Ellucian--所有大学生都不寒而栗--一样
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.96,0:15:46.41,CN,,0,0,0,,爱彼迎（房屋出租住宿），优步（打车租车），Toast 信用卡
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.43,0:15:47.96,CN,,0,0,0,,还有汉堡王？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.99,0:15:51.33,CN,,0,0,0,,他们是......Whopper Bar 等伟大创意的鼻祖
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.35,0:15:53.89,CN,,0,0,0,,根据营销总裁的说法，他们...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.91,0:15:56.57,CN,,0,0,0,,就像 Pimp My Ride 但为了汉堡？？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.23,0:15:59.23,CN,,0,0,0,,{\pos(969.33,925.33)\fscx61\fscy77}*Pimp My Ride：疯狂改装车，嘻哈改车族。真人秀电视节目，2004年播出，选一些很老很旧的车进行外观内饰等重新改造*
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.59,0:15:57.82,CN,,0,0,0,,闭上甜蜜的嘴吧
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.85,0:16:00.36,CN,,0,0,0,,嘿汉堡老板，你能不能给我的 Whopper
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.39,0:16:02.79,CN,,0,0,0,,加点额外的鳄梨酱呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.81,0:16:04.10,CN,,0,0,0,,Thank you! Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.13,0:16:05.15,CN,,0,0,0,,我们讲哪到了？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.18,0:16:06.02,CN,,0,0,0,,Oh, 对对对
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.04,0:16:08.79,CN,,0,0,0,,他们从 Twitch 手中买下了 Curse Media 的整个部门
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.82,0:16:11.45,CN,,0,0,0,,他们似乎真的只是为了维基
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.47,0:16:16.45,CN,,0,0,0,,由于我的世界论坛资金短缺，在这次出售后的短短四个月内
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.48,0:16:19.08,CN,,0,0,0,,他们就宣布整个网站将被归档
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.11,0:16:22.66,CN,,0,0,0,,作为回应，Mojang 删除了 “woo, minecraftforum!”的闪烁标语
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.69,0:16:24.28,CN,,0,0,0,,因为它没有意义了
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.31,0:16:26.55,CN,,0,0,0,,就在即将存档的前四天
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.58,0:16:28.83,CN,,0,0,0,,Minecraft 论坛被卖给了 Magic Find
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.85,0:16:30.61,CN,,0,0,0,,也就是今天的 Magic Find
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.63,0:16:33.79,CN,,0,0,0,,遗憾的是，Mojang 从未重新添加闪烁标语
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.82,0:16:39.03,CN,,0,0,0,,这将是 2018 年末被 Fandom 收购的许多非维基财产的命运
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.06,0:16:40.41,CN,,0,0,0,,要么烂掉
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.43,0:16:41.98,CN,,0,0,0,,要么卖给另一家公司
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.01,0:16:44.55,CN,,0,0,0,,这是非常标准的私募股权投资类型
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.58,0:16:47.79,CN,,0,0,0,,如果让他们损失一分钱，那就没戏了
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.82,0:16:49.97,CN,,0,0,0,,我是说，他们总得把钱还给银行
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.99,0:16:51.14,CN,,0,0,0,,不过，对于真正的维基来说
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.16,0:16:53.12,CN,,0,0,0,,他们希望保留这些维基
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.14,0:16:54.85,CN,,0,0,0,,出售发生在 2018 年底
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.88,0:16:58.40,CN,,0,0,0,,所有的 Gamepedia wiki 都将在他们的旧网站上保留一段时间
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.42,0:16:59.40,CN,,0,0,0,,在接下来的两年中
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.43,0:17:01.89,CN,,0,0,0,,他们将慢慢合并所有维基
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.92,0:17:05.29,CN,,0,0,0,,这一切在 2021 年 11 月 4 日达到了顶峰
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.31,0:17:09.05,CN,,0,0,0,,当时 Fandom 宣布所有 Gamepedia 和 Fandom 维基
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.08,0:17:10.49,CN,,0,0,0,,将被强行合并
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.52,0:17:11.77,CN,,0,0,0,,无论他们是否愿意
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.80,0:17:15.88,CN,,0,0,0,,正如我们之前提到的，Wikia-Fandom 上已经有了大量的维基
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.91,0:17:20.31,CN,,0,0,0,,这包括 minecraft.fandom.com 上的另一个我的世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.33,0:17:22.11,CN,,0,0,0,,那么，哪一个是真的呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.14,0:17:23.69,CN,,0,0,0,,Gamepedia 的那个是
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.72,0:17:25.84,CN,,0,0,0,,因为它实际上是官方的
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.86,0:17:28.90,CN,,0,0,0,,由于它也是更新更快、更受认可的维基
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.93,0:17:32.52,CN,,0,0,0,,所以 Fandom 维基不得不忍痛割爱，加入 Gamepedia 维基
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.54,0:17:38.05,CN,,0,0,0,,旧的 Fandom 维基将存档并移至 minecraft-archive.fandom.com
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.07,0:17:41.71,CN,,0,0,0,,Gamepedia 维基将移至 minecraft.fandom.com
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.73,0:17:43.62,CN,,0,0,0,,成为新的 Fandom 维基
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.64,0:17:47.57,CN,,0,0,0,,任何指向 minecraftwiki.net 或 minecraft.gamepedia.com
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.59,0:17:52.69,CN,,0,0,0,,或 minecraft.wikia.com 的链接都将重定向到新的 Fandom 维基上的相关页面
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.72,0:17:55.41,CN,,0,0,0,,这就是我们一开始看到的两个搜索结果
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.43,0:17:58.55,CN,,0,0,0,,还有 哇 这难道不美丽吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.57,0:18:00.67,CN,,0,0,0,,哇 太震撼了
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.22,0:18:02.21,CN,,0,0,0,,就像电击枪一样
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.23,0:18:03.72,CN,,0,0,0,,我是说，看看这个该死的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.75,0:18:06.24,CN,,0,0,0,,它基本上是 Pimp My Ride，但用于广告
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.26,0:18:07.38,CN,,0,0,0,,网站加载很慢
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.41,0:18:10.31,CN,,0,0,0,,还有一些愚蠢的测验、标签、侧边栏
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.34,0:18:13.60,CN,,0,0,0,,视频广告、推荐页面和一堆其他垃圾
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.63,0:18:16.95,CN,,0,0,0,,试图把你的注意力从维基上的内容上转移开
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.97,0:18:19.83,CN,,0,0,0,,总的来说，光是看着这东西就让我很难过
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.86,0:18:22.87,CN,,0,0,0,,维基应该是向公众提供信息的
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.90,0:18:25.71,CN,,0,0,0,,它应该是一本在线百科全书
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.74,0:18:29.69,CN,,0,0,0,,想象一下，你打开一本百科全书，在你想要的信息的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.72,0:18:31.59,CN,,0,0,0,,你会看到一个该死的大广告
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.62,0:18:35.63,CN,,0,0,0,,我认为重要的是，信息要保持自由，人人都能获取
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.65,0:18:38.99,CN,,0,0,0,,而像 Fandom 这样的公司却完全违背了这一点
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.02,0:18:42.59,CN,,0,0,0,,是的，Fandom的确让创建维基变得更容易
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.61,0:18:45.15,CN,,0,0,0,,但他们的行为却一再让维基上的
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.18,0:18:48.53,CN,,0,0,0,,实际信息变得更难获取
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.56,0:18:49.73,CN,,0,0,0,,也许只是我的问题
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.75,0:18:53.04,CN,,0,0,0,,但我不认为 Fandom 是为了让世界变得更好
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.07,0:18:55.60,CN,,0,0,0,,他们并不是要改进维基格式
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.63,0:18:58.64,CN,,0,0,0,,他们是一家私募股权公司旗下的营利性公司
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.66,0:19:02.03,CN,,0,0,0,,我想，也许，他们是想赚钱。但我不确定
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.05,0:19:04.11,CN,,0,0,0,,在我看来，这辆出租车确实很正常
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.13,0:19:06.88,CN,,0,0,0,,我想说的是，我理解所有的维基都不可能
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.90,0:19:09.89,CN,,0,0,0,,像维基百科那样是完美的、无广告的乌托邦
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.92,0:19:12.78,CN,,0,0,0,,但你可以通过广告持续运行一个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.80,0:19:15.31,CN,,0,0,0,,而不是让它看起来像这样，好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.34,0:19:16.74,CN,,0,0,0,,广告的观点从
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.76,0:19:19.38,CN,,0,0,0,,“哦，我们这样做只是为了支持服务器成本 ”
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.40,0:19:21.71,CN,,0,0,0,,到 “我们这样做是因为我们想要钱”
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.74,0:19:24.69,CN,,0,0,0,,我认为 Fandom 已经远远超过了这个点
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.72,0:19:28.28,CN,,0,0,0,,我的意思是，Fandom 创立之初，盈利能力基本上就是它的卖点
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.30,0:19:32.36,CN,,0,0,0,,维基百科唯一的创始人 Jimmy Wales（绝对相信我，bro）
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.39,0:19:35.19,CN,,0,0,0,,坐在他家周围茂密的丛林中
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.21,0:19:36.12,CN,,0,0,0,,问自己
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.14,0:19:38.45,CN,,0,0,0,,“如果我能靠这个赚钱呢？”
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.48,0:19:40.90,CN,,0,0,0,,答案很可能是 “那就糟透了”
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.18,0:19:44.98,CN,,0,0,0,,于是，维基城市诞生了
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.00,0:19:46.68,CN,,0,0,0,,它是 GeoCities 的翻版
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.71,0:19:51.11,CN,,0,0,0,,GeoCities 允许没有代码经验的人创建自己的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.14,0:19:54.49,CN,,0,0,0,,同样，Wikicities 也可以帮助人们创建自己的维基网站
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.52,0:19:58.34,CN,,0,0,0,,它们诞生于人们还知道 GeoCities 是什么的时代
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.37,0:19:59.95,CN,,0,0,0,,如今依然存在
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.97,0:20:03.79,CN,,0,0,0,,缓慢而坚定地将互联网变成一个越来越封闭的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.82,0:20:05.93,CN,,0,0,0,,这里不是任何人都能做自己的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.96,0:20:08.94,CN,,0,0,0,,而是只有大公司才能做自己的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.97,0:20:11.09,CN,,0,0,0,,维基代表着
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.12,0:20:14.61,CN,,0,0,0,,充满希望、自由信息、连接和独立的田园互联网
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.64,0:20:17.78,CN,,0,0,0,,而 Fandom 代表着我们所处的现实互联网：
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.80,0:20:22.31,CN,,0,0,0,,一个由大公司、围墙花园和大量广告组成的互联网
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.34,0:20:26.14,CN,,0,0,0,,有时，我们会觉得自己只能随波逐流
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.17,0:20:30.76,CN,,0,0,0,,任人宰割，并继续感到作为互联网公民的无能为力
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.68,0:20:33.36,CN,,0,0,0,,但幸运的是
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.38,0:20:35.36,CN,,0,0,0,,我们还是有办法解决这个问题的
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.55,0:20:41.87,CN,,0,0,0,,此维基 minecraft.fandom.com
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.90,0:20:44.02,CN,,0,0,0,,严格来说并不是官方维基
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.05,0:20:46.18,CN,,0,0,0,,现在已经没有官方维基了
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.21,0:20:49.30,CN,,0,0,0,,当 Dremelmoth 与他们续约时
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.33,0:20:52.66,CN,,0,0,0,,他们却说 “滚蛋”，并向他们提出了一大堆要求
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.68,0:20:54.52,CN,,0,0,0,,我希望这一个半字是值得的
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.54,0:20:58.68,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你想从 2009 年的原始我的世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.70,0:21:00.19,CN,,0,0,0,,直接画到这个 Fandom 的线
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.22,0:21:01.30,CN,,0,0,0,,那么，这就是我们刚刚所做的
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.32,0:21:04.46,CN,,0,0,0,,都是同一个维基，只是换了无数个主人而已
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.48,0:21:07.96,CN,,0,0,0,,这就是为什么 2009 年的这个链接仍然可以让你进入维基
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.99,0:21:10.34,CN,,0,0,0,,但是，如果我们看一下之前的搜索结果
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.36,0:21:12.77,CN,,0,0,0,,我们实际上看到了神秘的第三个 wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.79,0:21:16.13,CN,,0,0,0,,这是在一个完全不同的网站 minecraft.wiki 上
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.16,0:21:20.58,CN,,0,0,0,,它看起来更像维基百科，都是最新的，所有的合成都在那里
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.61,0:21:24.35,CN,,0,0,0,,我是说，我是说，看看它 没有广告
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.38,0:21:28.54,CN,,0,0,0,,整个屏幕都没有广告，这太疯狂了！我都不知道还有这种可能！
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.56,0:21:30.78,CN,,0,0,0,,这个好太多了，搞什么鬼？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.80,0:21:32.38,CN,,0,0,0,,为什么这是第三个结果？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.41,0:21:36.31,CN,,0,0,0,,为什么 Fandom 维基仍然存在，而这个看起来要好得多？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.34,0:21:39.74,CN,,0,0,0,,要理解这一点，我们必须了解维基的工作原理
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.76,0:21:43.31,CN,,0,0,0,,在这段视频中，我多次提到有人 “拥有 ”维基
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.34,0:21:45.70,CN,,0,0,0,,但我真正的意思是
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.73,0:21:49.81,CN,,0,0,0,,他们拥有运行维基网站服务器的责任
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.84,0:21:53.81,CN,,0,0,0,,他们控制着维基的品牌，拥有维基的域名
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.83,0:21:55.15,CN,,0,0,0,,让 Fandom 非常懊恼的是
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.18,0:21:56.73,CN,,0,0,0,,你无法购买事实
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.76,0:21:58.24,CN,,0,0,0,,至于维基上的文字内容
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.27,0:22:00.88,CN,,0,0,0,,则由人们自己决定
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.91,0:22:03.73,CN,,0,0,0,,正因为如此，我的世界维基上的人们
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.76,0:22:07.30,CN,,0,0,0,,开始进行一些关于......也许会离开 Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.33,0:22:08.90,CN,,0,0,0,,就在没人预料到他的时候
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.92,0:22:10.05,CN,,0,0,0,,Grimace 出手了
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.07,0:22:11.52,CN,,0,0,0,,是的，我是认真的
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.55,0:22:13.40,CN,,0,0,0,,2023年6月14日
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.42,0:22:17.02,CN,,0,0,0,,麦当劳用他们的3级gyatt和一些Fanum税来吸引Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.04,0:22:19.63,CN,,0,0,0,,在麦当劳的主要skibidi页面上
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.66,0:22:22.08,CN,,0,0,0,,进行了一次shillmaxxing广告，宣传Grimace奶昔
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.11,0:22:25.04,CN,,0,0,0,,维基上的红丸sigma被迫吞食glizzies
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.07,0:22:28.89,CN,,0,0,0,,而Shadow Wizard Money Gang则以ocky方式在袋子里放广告
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.91,0:22:32.17,CN,,0,0,0,,这让他们对opps非常怀疑，失去了很多光环
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.20,0:22:33.06,CN,,0,0,0,,这是最后一根稻草——
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.09,0:22:34.57,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你理解我刚才说的话
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.59,0:22:35.73,CN,,0,0,0,,请今天出去走走
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.75,0:22:37.65,CN,,0,0,0,,对许多人来说，这是最后一根稻草
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.67,0:22:39.95,CN,,0,0,0,,因为它向Fandom上的每个社区表明
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.98,0:22:42.60,CN,,0,0,0,,现在对他们来说没有什么神圣的东西了
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.63,0:22:45.45,CN,,0,0,0,,维基的任何部分，甚至一个锁定的首页
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.48,0:22:49.27,CN,,0,0,0,,现在都可以在几乎没有通知的情况下被强行更改为广告
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.30,0:22:52.10,CN,,0,0,0,,虽然这不太可能发生在像我的世界这样的游戏上
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.13,0:22:54.14,CN,,0,0,0,,但令人担忧的是先例
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.16,0:22:56.67,CN,,0,0,0,,现在，维基的意义到底是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.70,0:23:00.06,CN,,0,0,0,,整个东西都属于Fandom，他们只是改变了它！
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.09,0:23:01.96,CN,,0,0,0,,借助Grimace事件的火药
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.99,0:23:04.30,CN,,0,0,0,,人们更愿意谈论
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.32,0:23:05.83,CN,,0,0,0,,离开这个该死的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.86,0:23:08.43,CN,,0,0,0,,这已经在Discord服务器上引起了很大的关注
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.46,0:23:11.73,CN,,0,0,0,,由于他们这次真的非常认真
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.75,0:23:14.74,CN,,0,0,0,,他们将讨论转移到维基上的讨论页面
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.77,0:23:17.06,CN,,0,0,0,,以获取不使用Discord的人的意见
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.08,0:23:18.50,CN,,0,0,0,,是时候离开这里了
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.53,0:23:20.62,CN,,0,0,0,,……但是，实际上你怎么做到这一点呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.64,0:23:22.96,CN,,0,0,0,,信不信由你，Fandom 实际上有一整页
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.98,0:23:24.86,CN,,0,0,0,,关于如何打包离开
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.89,0:23:25.99,CN,,0,0,0,,称之为分支
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.01,0:23:27.55,CN,,0,0,0,,（因为勺子已经被拿走了）
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.58,0:23:31.07,CN,,0,0,0,,就是在旧版本的基础上开始新版本的过程
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.09,0:23:32.18,CN,,0,0,0,,不过，当你分支时
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.21,0:23:33.97,CN,,0,0,0,,他们有三大规则
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.99,0:23:35.23,CN,,0,0,0,,你不能破坏旧维基
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.25,0:23:37.63,CN,,0,0,0,,不能在旧维基上宣传新维基
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.66,0:23:39.91,CN,,0,0,0,,而且管理员只能管理其中一个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.94,0:23:42.28,CN,,0,0,0,,这些都使得离开 Fandom 更加困难
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.30,0:23:45.05,CN,,0,0,0,,因为旧的 Fandom 维基必须继续存在
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.08,0:23:47.48,CN,,0,0,0,,并与你创建的新维基竞争
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.50,0:23:51.68,CN,,0,0,0,,如果这是一个真正的分支，这些规则是人们自然而然地会做的事情
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.71,0:23:53.99,CN,,0,0,0,,因为两个维基都在积极开发中
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.02,0:23:57.65,CN,,0,0,0,,但如果你想把整个维基从 Fandom 上移走，他们会让你很为难
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.67,0:24:00.33,CN,,0,0,0,,然后在页面底部，他们发出了最后的恳求：
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.35,0:24:03.28,CN,,0,0,0,,“求求你，求求你留在 Fandom 上吧！
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.31,0:24:06.17,CN,,0,0,0,,我们编起来太难了…
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.20,0:24:07.60,CN,,0,0,0,,因为我们这么说......”
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.62,0:24:09.05,CN,,0,0,0,,因此，一场公投开始了
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.08,0:24:13.88,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上，请排出你的分支首选，留在 Fandom 也是一种选择
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.91,0:24:17.60,CN,,0,0,0,,这实际上是严肃的，每个人都可以，嗯...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.63,0:24:20.20,CN,,0,0,0,,表达他们对 Fandom 的真实感受
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.22,0:24:22.87,CN,,0,0,0,,-“ Fandom 太可怕了，任何东西都是升级版”
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.90,0:24:25.45,CN,,0,0,0,,“不断出现的广告以及干扰性的边栏
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.48,0:24:27.79,CN,,0,0,0,,让人很难使用该网站”
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.81,0:24:29.92,CN,,0,0,0,,——“维基托管变得越来越不稳定
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.94,0:24:32.12,CN,,0,0,0,,有争议的创新被强加
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.15,0:24:35.63,CN,,0,0,0,,而长期存在的问题没有得到更新或删除”
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.66,0:24:39.06,CN,,0,0,0,,“广告的海洋，广告本身具有
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.08,0:24:43.10,CN,,0,0,0,,侵略性的宣传性质。为了广告而取消年龄的匿名化”
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.13,0:24:45.57,CN,,0,0,0,,“结果，这不再是一个维基农场，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.59,0:24:47.43,CN,,0,0,0,,而是一个广告平台”
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.45,0:24:50.45,CN,,0,0,0,,——“在Gamepedia下有一种安全感和稳定性
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.48,0:24:53.24,CN,,0,0,0,,我认为这种感觉得并没有随着迁移到Fandom而延续”
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.26,0:24:56.79,CN,,0,0,0,,-“Fandom的行为表明，它关注的是利润，而不是质量
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.82,0:25:00.83,CN,,0,0,0,,和编辑自由，这有损于本维基。该走了”
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.85,0:25:04.23,CN,,0,0,0,,-“总的来说，只要我们能把分支分到Fandom以外的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.26,0:25:05.82,CN,,0,0,0,,我就会对结果感到满意”
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.85,0:25:07.65,CN,,0,0,0,,因此，虽然最好的选择并不明确
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.67,0:25:09.79,CN,,0,0,0,,但最坏的选择肯定是明确的
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.81,0:25:12.10,CN,,0,0,0,,所以，不出意外的话，分支是会出现的
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.12,0:25:13.99,CN,,0,0,0,,但是，我们要把分支分到哪里去呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.02,0:25:15.37,CN,,0,0,0,,又是个好问题
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.39,0:25:18.43,CN,,0,0,0,,他们基本上可以选择任何他们想要的维基农场
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.46,0:25:20.18,CN,,0,0,0,,但主要有四个选项
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.20,0:25:23.26,CN,,0,0,0,,wiki.gg是一个非常受欢迎的Fandom替代
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.29,0:25:25.61,CN,,0,0,0,,目前，他们拥有近千个维基
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.63,0:25:27.05,CN,,0,0,0,,包括一些游戏如
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.08,0:25:29.25,CN,,0,0,0,,《泰拉瑞亚》、《雨中冒险》、《疯狂连杀》等游戏的维基
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.28,0:25:30.12,CN,,0,0,0,,当然还有
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.14,0:25:31.56,CN,,0,0,0,,Hello Kitty岛冒险
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.59,0:25:35.14,CN,,0,0,0,,很多人喜欢他们，因为他们是由 Gamepedia 的前员工经营的
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.17,0:25:37.54,CN,,0,0,0,,包括我们的老朋友 Donovan Duncan！
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.57,0:25:39.46,CN,,0,0,0,,但这只是表明，这个选项
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.49,0:25:40.40,CN,,0,0,0,,归根结底
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.43,0:25:42.28,CN,,0,0,0,,只是另一个公司的维基农场
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.30,0:25:45.78,CN,,0,0,0,,就像再一次答应 Donovan，那就......有点怪怪的
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.80,0:25:49.19,CN,,0,0,0,,也许去那里会让这一切重演
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.21,0:25:53.58,CN,,0,0,0,,他们还考虑了不那么企业化的公司，即 StrategyWiki 的托管公司 ABXY
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.61,0:25:55.65,CN,,0,0,0,,这是他们的网站，额...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.68,0:25:57.91,CN,,0,0,0,,这甚至还不是 Web 1.0
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.93,0:25:59.01,CN,,0,0,0,,这就像 CERN
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.93,0:26:02.93,CN,,0,0,0,,{\pos(952,926)}*CERN：这里指世界上第一个网站 http://info.cern.ch*
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.04,0:26:00.66,CN,,0,0,0,,他们几乎没有任何品牌标识
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.69,0:26:03.90,CN,,0,0,0,,只是在底部有一个小小的 “Powered By StrategyWiki”
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.92,0:26:05.65,CN,,0,0,0,,这几乎是太少的企业监督
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.68,0:26:08.35,CN,,0,0,0,,因为他们甚至没有全球内容交付网络
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.37,0:26:10.38,CN,,0,0,0,,所有的网页都托管在美国
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.41,0:26:13.27,CN,,0,0,0,,使世界其他地方的网站访问变慢
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.29,0:26:16.43,CN,,0,0,0,,尤其是我的世界维基有巨大的流量
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.46,0:26:20.42,CN,,0,0,0,,还有 Bulbagarden，它是 Bulbapedia 上神奇宝贝维基的主机
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.45,0:26:24.02,CN,,0,0,0,,据称，他们曾多次拒绝 Fandom 的收购要约
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.05,0:26:26.24,CN,,0,0,0,,但我找不到任何具体证据
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.27,0:26:28.29,CN,,0,0,0,,而且他们在这一领域拥有丰富的经验
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.31,0:26:31.09,CN,,0,0,0,,不过，它们不允许匿名编辑
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.12,0:26:33.20,CN,,0,0,0,,这让很多人望而却步
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.23,0:26:35.34,CN,,0,0,0,,有一家公司真的主动联系了他们： 
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.37,0:26:36.21,CN,,0,0,0,,Weird Gloop.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.24,0:26:39.48,CN,,0,0,0,,他们的名称和徽标是根据《RuneScape》的同名物品设计的
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.50,0:26:40.96,CN,,0,0,0,,还记得《RuneScape》维基
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.98,0:26:42.96,CN,,0,0,0,,如何因为视频广告而离开 Fandom 吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.99,0:26:43.91,CN,,0,0,0,,这就是他们
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.93,0:26:45.74,CN,,0,0,0,,虽然他们有一些不好的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.77,0:26:48.18,CN,,0,0,0,,比如他们对可以使用哪些小部件的奇怪规定
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.20,0:26:49.88,CN,,0,0,0,,但他们也有很多优势
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.90,0:26:50.96,CN,,0,0,0,,这是一家小公司
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.99,0:26:53.16,CN,,0,0,0,,他们的网站快速可靠
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.18,0:26:55.07,CN,,0,0,0,,他们有全职系统管理员
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.10,0:26:57.71,CN,,0,0,0,,并且对他们的商业实践非常透明
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.74,0:26:59.34,CN,,0,0,0,,他们还把钱花在了刀刃上
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.37,0:27:01.33,CN,,0,0,0,,买下了域名
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.35,0:27:02.96,CN,,0,0,0,,如果转用 Weird Gloop 的话就能得到
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.98,0:27:04.78,CN,,0,0,0,,在这一点上，他们和 Curse 非常相似
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.80,0:27:07.96,CN,,0,0,0,,竭尽全力确保自己成为主力
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.98,0:27:09.53,CN,,0,0,0,,在制作这段视频时
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.55,0:27:13.26,CN,,0,0,0,,他们的经营方式似乎非常专业
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.28,0:27:15.23,CN,,0,0,0,,看起来，他们真的知道自己在做什么
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.25,0:27:19.55,CN,,0,0,0,,所有这些方案都有各自的优缺点，其中 Weird Gloop 略占上风
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.58,0:27:21.74,CN,,0,0,0,,但所有这些方案都有一个无法回避的问题
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.77,0:27:23.88,CN,,0,0,0,,这也是我们开始讨论这件事的初衷：
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.90,0:27:25.07,CN,,0,0,0,,搜索结果排名
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.09,0:27:28.24,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上，据我所知，有一种东西叫 SEO
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.27,0:27:30.04,CN,,0,0,0,,即搜索引擎优化
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.06,0:27:32.03,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上，可以做很多事情
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.05,0:27:35.24,CN,,0,0,0,,来让网站在搜索结果中显示得更高
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.26,0:27:37.22,CN,,0,0,0,,排在首页是非常强大的
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.24,0:27:39.35,CN,,0,0,0,,成为第一个链接是我们的目标
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.38,0:27:41.34,CN,,0,0,0,,如何提高搜索引擎优化？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.05,0:27:46.39,CN,,0,0,0,,这就是有趣的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.41,0:27:48.41,CN,,0,0,0,,没个人知道！！
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.44,0:27:50.98,CN,,0,0,0,,好吧，谷歌有一篇关于搜索引擎优化的文章
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.00,0:27:52.36,CN,,0,0,0,,其中提供了一些一般性建议
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.39,0:27:55.03,CN,,0,0,0,,但至于某种神奇的登顶方法
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.06,0:27:56.53,CN,,0,0,0,,那是不存在的
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.06,0:27:57.06,CN,,0,0,0,,{\pos(1668,908)}*HAF：得加钱*
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.55,0:27:58.53,CN,,0,0,0,,因为如果这样做了，每个人都会这么做
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.55,0:28:02.21,CN,,0,0,0,,公司花重金聘请被称为搜索引擎优化专家的人
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.24,0:28:06.09,CN,,0,0,0,,他们的唯一目的就是为搜索引擎优化网站
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.11,0:28:09.55,CN,,0,0,0,,一般来说，他似乎优先考虑规模更大、相互关联的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.57,0:28:13.00,CN,,0,0,0,,这些网站内容更丰富、链接更多，访问者花费的时间也更长
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.03,0:28:17.52,CN,,0,0,0,,而 Fandom 恰好是访问量最大的 50 个网站之一
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.54,0:28:18.71,CN,,0,0,0,,在全世界
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.74,0:28:19.85,CN,,0,0,0,,我觉得你不明白
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.88,0:28:21.45,CN,,0,0,0,,Fandom 很受欢迎
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.48,0:28:22.94,CN,,0,0,0,,比天气网还TM欢迎
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.97,0:28:23.85,CN,,0,0,0,,正如我们前面所看到的
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.87,0:28:27.01,CN,,0,0,0,,这意味着它经常被放在搜索结果的最前面
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.03,0:28:29.22,CN,,0,0,0,,尽管它比其他选项差
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.25,0:28:31.24,CN,,0,0,0,,在合并之前，人们最担心的就是
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.26,0:28:35.12,CN,,0,0,0,,即使他们费尽周折把维基转移到另一个网站上
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.15,0:28:38.56,CN,,0,0,0,,Fandom 的结果也会把他们扼杀在摇篮里，那一切就都白费了
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.59,0:28:42.79,CN,,0,0,0,,不过，其中有一家公司确实在搜索结果中击败了 Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.82,0:28:44.13,CN,,0,0,0,,他就是 Weird Gloop
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.16,0:28:48.22,CN,,0,0,0,,RuneScape 维基成功地在结果中超越了 Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.24,0:28:49.88,CN,,0,0,0,,这是非常有意义的
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.91,0:28:51.21,CN,,0,0,0,,有了这些优点
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.23,0:28:52.88,CN,,0,0,0,,Weird Gloop 一经推出
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.91,0:28:56.07,CN,,0,0,0,,就迅速成为维基上人们的最爱
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.09,0:28:57.10,CN,,0,0,0,,（在Fandom 上）进行了一次大投票
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.13,0:29:01.38,CN,,0,0,0,,决定由 Weird Gloop 托管新的我的世界维基
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.41,0:29:04.45,CN,,0,0,0,,为了确保他们不得不再次这样做会更容易
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.48,0:29:08.15,CN,,0,0,0,,我的世界维基的人们有一份与 Weird Gloop 的协议清单
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.17,0:29:11.07,CN,,0,0,0,,这是为我的世界维基上的每个人编写的
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.09,0:29:12.34,CN,,0,0,0,,（当然，链接在简介中）
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.37,0:29:15.04,CN,,0,0,0,,基本上，如果任何一方想退出，他们都可以离开
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.06,0:29:17.44,CN,,0,0,0,,Weird Gloop 将提供 minecraft.wiki 域名
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.47,0:29:19.27,CN,,0,0,0,,给社区中值得信赖的人
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.29,0:29:21.40,CN,,0,0,0,,向他们提供维基中包含的所有数据
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.43,0:29:23.59,CN,,0,0,0,,他们基本上可以用它做任何他们想做的事情
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.62,0:29:27.53,CN,,0,0,0,,现在，剩下要做的就是把所有东西都搬一遍
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.17,0:29:32.17,CN,,0,0,0,,2023 年 9 月 24 日
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.19,0:29:35.53,CN,,0,0,0,,该维基已正式分支为 minecraft.wiki
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.55,0:29:37.52,CN,,0,0,0,,虽然 Fandom 维基仍然存在
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.55,0:29:41.62,CN,,0,0,0,,但几乎所有在 Fandom 维基上工作过的人都转移到了新维基上
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.64,0:29:42.91,CN,,0,0,0,,实际上，这意味着
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.94,0:29:45.97,CN,,0,0,0,,与 Minecraft 维基相比，它看起来基本上是不完整的
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.99,0:29:47.71,CN,,0,0,0,,尤其是在新功能方面
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.73,0:29:50.56,CN,,0,0,0,,维基分支已经有一年多了
Dialogue: 0,0:29:50.59,0:29:53.48,CN,,0,0,0,,他们的表现实际上比在 Fandom 上的表现要好得多
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.51,0:29:56.94,CN,,0,0,0,,他们最近发表了一篇关于他们独立第一年的文章
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.96,0:29:58.67,CN,,0,0,0,,这表明——信不信由你——
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.69,0:30:03.20,CN,,0,0,0,,在一个不会每时每刻都有大量广告轰炸的网站上
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.23,0:30:04.77,CN,,0,0,0,,人们会更愿意访问你的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.79,0:30:06.22,CN,,0,0,0,,我知道，这有点疯狂！
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.24,0:30:07.95,CN,,0,0,0,,虽然正如我们之前看到的那样
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.98,0:30:10.57,CN,,0,0,0,,许多搜索结果仍然将 Fandom 放在首位
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.60,0:30:13.37,CN,,0,0,0,,但就大多数新功能而言，新维基胜出
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.39,0:30:15.96,CN,,0,0,0,,就像之前 Redstone Wire Ltd 的情况一样
Dialogue: 0,0:30:15.99,0:30:18.28,CN,,0,0,0,,现在有一家公司负责管理维基：
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.31,0:30:19.66,CN,,0,0,0,,Block & Quill Ltd.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.69,0:30:21.13,CN,,0,0,0,,他们有两个常设职位
Dialogue: 0,0:30:21.15,0:30:23.65,CN,,0,0,0,,以及五个民选的董事会成员职位
Dialogue: 0,0:30:23.67,0:30:25.70,CN,,0,0,0,,这些职位每年都要通过
Dialogue: 0,0:30:25.73,0:30:27.70,CN,,0,0,0,,舒尔茨方法进行排序选择投票选举
Dialogue: 0,0:30:25.73,0:30:29.73,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fscx68\fscy78\pos(974,942)}*Schulze method：舒尔茨方法，一种选举机制，最终会产生一位获胜者。机制过于复杂这里不多讲述*
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.72,0:30:29.19,CN,,0,0,0,,因为他们都是书呆子
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.21,0:30:30.38,CN,,0,0,0,,我不太清楚这是怎么运作的
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.40,0:30:33.60,CN,,0,0,0,,但我认为CGP Grey随时都会制作一个视频来解释
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.62,0:30:35.88,CN,,0,0,0,,有些人仍然在Fandom维基上
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.90,0:30:39.61,CN,,0,0,0,,只是防止破坏行为并非常缓慢地添加内容
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.64,0:30:40.74,CN,,0,0,0,,这没关系
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.76,0:30:41.60,CN,,0,0,0,,我还应该提到--
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.62,0:30:44.66,CN,,0,0,0,,请不要破坏我在视频中提到的任何维基
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.69,0:30:47.94,CN,,0,0,0,,一个真正的人必须去解决这个问题
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.96,0:30:50.91,CN,,0,0,0,,破坏维基丝毫无损于 Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.94,0:30:52.39,CN,,0,0,0,,所以......请不要这样做
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.42,0:30:54.30,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你真的想伤害 Fandom
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.32,0:30:57.09,CN,,0,0,0,,最好的办法就是停止使用他们的网站
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.11,0:30:59.80,CN,,0,0,0,,你可以不在搜索结果中选择它
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.83,0:31:02.81,CN,,0,0,0,,或者使用一个名为 Indie Wiki Buddy 的 Chrome 浏览器扩展
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.84,0:31:06.53,CN,,0,0,0,,它将所有 Fandom 维基重定向到其独立的替代维基
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.56,0:31:08.70,CN,,0,0,0,,不是赞助，只是一个很好的扩展
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.72,0:31:12.21,CN,,0,0,0,,不管是我的世界还是 RuneScape 或任何这些游戏
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.24,0:31:14.01,CN,,0,0,0,,它都会将你重定向到正确的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.04,0:31:17.04,CN,,0,0,0,,所以查找 “我的世界 红石 ”会显示如下
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.06,0:31:20.97,CN,,0,0,0,,链接已灰显，并链接到独立维基上的相同文章
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.99,0:31:23.49,CN,,0,0,0,,它实际上会为你重新排列搜索结果
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.52,0:31:26.50,CN,,0,0,0,,这在制作这个视频时有点恼人
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.53,0:31:28.96,CN,,0,0,0,,但在正常游戏中可能会对你有用
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.98,0:31:31.64,CN,,0,0,0,,还有一个为实际游戏制作的模组
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.67,0:31:35.33,CN,,0,0,0,,它会在维基站点上为你正在查看的区块或物品打开一个选项卡
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.35,0:31:36.53,CN,,0,0,0,,在你按下 H 键时显示
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.55,0:31:38.76,CN,,0,0,0,,这不完全是我的节奏，但我想我应该提到它
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.78,0:31:39.90,CN,,0,0,0,,另外，我想说的是
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.92,0:31:42.41,CN,,0,0,0,,如果你对维基的更多历史感兴趣
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.43,0:31:44.74,CN,,0,0,0,,包括很多我无法在这里介绍的东西
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.77,0:31:46.99,CN,,0,0,0,,你应该去看看维基上的这个页面
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.01,0:31:49.16,CN,,0,0,0,,在制作这段视频的过程中，它非常有用
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.18,0:31:52.19,CN,,0,0,0,,可以随时了解当时的大致情况
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.21,0:31:54.22,CN,,0,0,0,,制作页面的人 TreeIsLife 也非常热心
Dialogue: 0,0:31:54.25,0:31:56.43,CN,,0,0,0,,帮我查看了视频台词
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.45,0:31:58.22,CN,,0,0,0,,既然说到翻看视频台词
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.25,0:32:01.49,CN,,0,0,0,,我也要感谢 Harristic 翻看了关于分支的部分
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.51,0:32:04.21,CN,,0,0,0,,他们都对这个维基提供了很多个人经验
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.24,0:32:07.16,CN,,0,0,0,,我非常感谢他们抽出时间来帮助我
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.80,0:32:33.63,CN,,0,0,0,,Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.65,0:32:36.27,CN,,0,0,0,,我想在圣诞节前把这段视频放出来...
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.81,0:32:38.49,CN,,0,0,0,,但是没办到
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.51,0:32:40.73,CN,,0,0,0,,因为我现在在圣诞节录制它
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.98,0:32:45.41,CN,,0,0,0,,所以我们就假装这个场景是为宽扎节装饰的
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.98,0:32:46.98,CN,,0,0,0,,{\pos(962,940)}*Kwanzaa：宽扎节，果实初收节，是非裔美国人的节日\N庆祝活动共七天，从12月26日至1月1日*
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.43,0:32:46.28,CN,,0,0,0,,好吗？(●'◡'●)
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.30,0:32:51.46,CN,,0,0,0,,我非常感谢今年我在这个频道上所做的一切
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.27,0:32:53.52,CN,,0,0,0,,这真是太棒了......
Dialogue: 0,0:32:54.24,0:32:57.12,CN,,0,0,0,,......看到人们真正喜欢我所做的事情
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.15,0:32:59.17,CN,,0,0,0,,我没有接受过视频剪辑方面的培训
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.20,0:33:02.67,CN,,0,0,0,,也没有接受过写作或其他方面的培训......
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.84,0:33:03.09,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(1602,924)}小学不算\N因为它让我写得更糟糕 {\fn思源黑体 CN Regular\fs90}:)
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.69,0:33:04.92,CN,,0,0,0,,我只是自学成才，而且......
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.94,0:33:06.70,CN,,0,0,0,,人们喜欢它。这对我意义重大
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.73,0:33:07.69,CN,,0,0,0,,说真的
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.71,0:33:08.73,CN,,0,0,0,,就像，我
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.25,0:33:10.46,CN,,0,0,0,,这— 这太疯狂了
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.38,0:33:13.28,CN,,0,0,0,,这太疯狂了
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.31,0:33:14.18,CN,,0,0,0,,还有
Dialogue: 0,0:33:14.92,0:33:17.18,CN,,0,0,0,,我不知道该说什么，真的
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.21,0:33:19.73,CN,,0,0,0,,我只是说我会打开摄像机
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.76,0:33:21.12,CN,,0,0,0,,然后开始说话，但是...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.84,0:33:25.80,CN,,0,0,0,,我......真的不知道该说什么
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.82,0:33:27.53,CN,,0,0,0,,编辑起来会很麻烦，抱歉 Dime
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.06,0:33:28.92,CN,,0,0,0,,总之
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.13,0:33:31.67,CN,,0,0,0,,谢谢。说真的
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.70,0:33:33.55,CN,,0,0,0,,圣诞快乐，新年快乐
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.89,0:33:35.90,CN,,0,0,0,,宽扎节...快乐
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.93,0:33:38.35,CN,,0,0,0,,这一套当然是为宽扎节装饰的
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.69,0:33:39.53,CN,,0,0,0,,很肯定的说
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.55,0:33:42.41,CN,,0,0,0,,只是......请关注我的更多内容
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.44,0:33:45.74,CN,,0,0,0,,我喜欢制作视频，我想一直制作下去
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.76,0:33:47.72,CN,,0,0,0,,我对这个频道的未来充满期待
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.75,0:33:52.04,CN,,0,0,0,,祝你冬至快乐，无论你的文化是什么
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.07,0:33:55.32,CN,,0,0,0,,失陪了，我得去拆礼物了
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.24,0:34:01.69,CN,,0,0,0,,欸，真不错 (๑╹◡╹๑)
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.69,0:33:35.69,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\fscx87\fscy92\pos(959.56,125.89)}原标题：The Minecraft Wiki vs Corporate Greed  原作者：DIMM4
Dialogue: 0,0:33:36.09,0:33:40.09,CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(961.56,129.89)}原视频上传日期：2024年12月30日
